const PRYD={"Hathor":{"slug":"hathor","skills":[{"t":"Basic Attack","n":"Rapid Delivery","d":"Basic Attack: Rapid Delivery Displays superior martial arts, performing up to 5 consecutive attacks, dealing Lakshana DMG . Basic Attack: Final Dispatch Press Basic Attack while airborne to plunge, dealing 1 instance of Lakshana DMG to an area upon impact. Increases DMG based on fall height, up to 100% . Basic Attack: To The Skies Hold Basic Attack to trigger combo branch attacks. Sweeps around the target at high speed to knock them up, then restrains and plunges, dealing 1 instance of Lakshana DMG to an area on impact. Performs Final Dispatch if the target cannot be knocked up. Critical Riposte: Zero-Error Operation Triggers when using Rapid Delivery after a Critical Dodge. Launches a lightning-fast counterattack, dealing 1 instance of Lakshana DMG to an area, reducing Break, and gaining Express Delivery Power on hit (up to 1 stack every 5 s). Legend speaks of a secret art mastered only by Elite Couriers who have completed tens of thousands of flawless deliveries. With an almost instinctive striking rhythm, they tear through any obstacle blocking the delivery route, all to ensure a single successful delivery without breaking promises or trust.","m":["1st Instance Ratio: 24.3%","2nd Instance Ratio: 16.1% + 13.6% ×4","3rd Instance Ratio: 13.3% ×2","4th Instance Ratio: 22.4% + 47.9% + 99.4%","5th Instance Ratio: 44.1% + 109.9%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Aerial Command","d":"Redirect Skill: Aerial Command Target locked, time to wrap this up quickly. Leaps into the air and slashes the target in front with wings, gaining 2 stacks of Express Delivery Power . Hold to enter charge status, increasing the power of Aerial Command and inflicting targets in range with Five-Star Tracking effect. The charge lasts up to 5 s, during which Hathor constantly deals AoE Lakshana DMG while the skill radius gradually expands. The effect ends when the skill button is released, concluding the charging phase. Lasts for 5 s. Grants 3 stacks of Express Delivery Power when the target attacks or hits Hathor or an ally during this time. Redirect Skill: Cyclone Strike Consumes Express Delivery Power to cast this skill while in Emergency Delivery status. Summons a motorcycle of thorns and inflicts a rapid combo on the target. To ensure delivery within the time limit, forcibly eliminating enemies along the way is also one of the basic principles of the job.","m":[]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Rider Express","d":"Get out of the way. Summons a motorcycle made of thorns and circles around targets, charging at enemies ahead with increased speed. Launches into the air and dive-bombs the ground, dealing 1 instance of Lakshana DMG to an area. Enters Emergency Delivery state for a period after skill activation and stops gaining Express Delivery Power . Upgrades Aerial Command to Cyclone Strike in this state. Increases Movement Speed and grants ATK bonus based on Express Delivery Power stacks. Ends Emergency Delivery state immediately when switching characters during this period. \"Faster. Faster. Faster — !\"","m":["DMG Ratio: 96.2% *2 + 507.6%","Emergency Delivery Duration: 5s","CD: 15s","Costs Ultimate Energy: 100","Movement Speed +: 30%"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Impact Point Designation","d":"The time has come. Strikes from the air, kicking the target to trigger an impact, dealing 2 instances of Lakshana DMG to an area. Right now.","m":["DMG Ratio: 63.9% + 136.1%"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Delay Warning","d":"Remora Enhancement : Extends the target\u0027s Remora duration to 12s and increases Crit Rate by 10% when attacking a target affected by Remora . Can\u0027t risk the delay. I\u0027ll handle it.","m":[]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Efficiency Boost","d":"Grants 1 stack of Express Delivery Power after defeating a target. I can go faster.","m":[]}],"how":"Hathor Hyper Hathor · Jiuyuan · Zero (MC) · Haniel A Charge-reaction team built around Hathor\u0027s Feather Stack (Express Delivery Power) loop and Emergency Delivery state, with Jiuyuan and MC enabling Blossom for the Charge triple-cycle. Rotation Jiuyuan: Start with Jiuyuan and use her Ultimate (Final Reckoning) and Redirect Skill. Zero (MC): Switch to MC to trigger Blossom and use their Ultimate. Haniel: Switch to Haniel and use her Redirect Skill (Silent Moonlit Forest Guardian) and Ultimate (A Melody Named Haniel) to apply the ATK and Crit Damage buff (at R6). Hathor: Swap to Hathor to trigger Stain and fully hold-charge her Redirect Skill (Aerial Command) to gain feathers (Express Delivery Power stacks). Hathor: Quick-Swap from Hathor to MC. Hathor: Swap back to Hathor to trigger Remora and Charge. Hathor: Immediately activate her Ultimate (Rider Express) to enter Emergency Delivery, then use her 3 enhanced Redirect Skills (Cyclone Strike). Zero (MC): During the animation of the 3rd Cyclone Strike, swap to MC and use Redirect Skill. Jiuyuan: Swap to Jiuyuan to trigger Blossom and subsequently Charge. Hathor: Return to Hathor to absorb Ultimate energy from the reaction. If Hathor\u0027s energy is full, swap to Haniel to generate Ultimate energy for her as well. Take time rebuilding energy and Cycle bar on Haniel. Repeat from the first step. Tips \u0026 Tricks When fighting enemies that can be affected by crowd control effects, Hathor can perform a Suplex with her Charged Basic Attack. You can fill Hathor\u0027s Cycle bar with one fully-charged Redirect Skill (Aerial Command) and two Charged Attacks. Her Redirect Skill (Aerial Command) can be released after 10 ticks and still grant the full feathers compared to holding for the maximum of 20 ticks.","pros":"Extremely high burst ceiling once she enters enhanced ultimate state, letting her defeat clustered enemies quickly. Very strong AoE value, thrives when there are multiple enemies to farm stacks from. Ultimate charges faster over time because stacking also feeds energy gain. High payoff character when you play around timing and counter windows correctly. Delivery Driver brrrr (Bonuses in the minigame + she can automatically complete 1 delivery per day. She unlocks the Hamster Ball in the house/apartments, which can give you free modules.","cons":"Very Ultimate locked, outside of it her damage drops a lot. Her ultimate can be hard to hit against moving bosses. Stack gain can be unreliable depending on enemy type and how often they attack. Really likes Charge.","teams":[{"n":"Remora Team","m":["zero","haniel","edgar"],"c":"This team can trigger both Remora and Stain to buff Hathor’s personal damage. The goal would be to trigger Stain and then Remora, to get as much damage under the 20% damage and 12% crit buffs as possible.","r":""},{"n":"Hathor Hypercarry Team","m":["jiuyuan, nanally, mint","hotori, zero","haniel, fadia"],"c":"This team can trigger both Stain and Charge. Ideally the order you would want to trigger things in is Blossom \u003e Stain \u003e Remora (Charge) with Hathor being the one to trigger the Charge reaction and stay on field for the energy. Additionally, if Hathor doesn’t need the energy, you can use this team to trigger Charge first and give Haniel energy for her Ultimate and then switch off of her onto Hathor for the maximum Stain duration.","r":""}]},"Sakiri":{"slug":"sakiri","skills":[{"t":"Basic Attack","n":"Kiroumaru Headbutt","d":"Ram Sakiri swings Kiroumaru and performs up to 5 consecutive attacks, dealing Incantation DMG . Eating Mode Hold to activate Eating Mode with Kiroumaru. Mounts Sakiri onto Kiroumaru, allowing movement. Opens its mouth to continuously pull nearby targets within a cone while Hungry. Destroys movable objects in the scene and devours weak enemies. Takes 180s to digest each devoured enemy, with only 1 target digested at a time. Becomes Full when the number of enemies being digested reaches the limit, remaining movable but unable to pull or devour enemies. Release to exit the mode. Swallow Wields Kiroumaru in the air and plunges, dealing 1 instance of Incantation DMG to an area upon impact. Increases DMG based on fall height, up to 100% . Critical Riposte: Mischief Triggers when using Ram after a Critical Dodge. Leaps high into the air and strikes down hard with Kiroumaru against enemies left vulnerable by their missed attacks. Deals 1 instance of Incantation DMG to an area and reduces Break. According to Mr. T, an oddity who survived the depths of Kiroumaru\u0027s belly and lived to tell the tale thanks to Sakiri\u0027s timely intervention, hints at an unexpected perk: Amidst the gloom, one might unearth a half-digested game console to while away the hours — a quirky, entertaining twist to an otherwise harrowing wait for rescue.","m":["1st Instance Ratio: 40.3%","2nd Instance Ratio: 13.8% + 75.7%","3rd Instance Ratio: 1.6% + 71.6%","4th Instance Ratio: 33.1% ×3","5th Instance Ratio: 3.5% + 106.2%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Devour Whole","d":"Burp Press to activate. Kiroumaru opens its mouth, pulling in nearby enemies. Kiroumaru then inflates and knocks down the enemy. Gravity Eater Hold to activate. Kiroumaru opens its mouth, pulling in nearby enemies. Kiroumaru then bites through the ground, devouring the gravity in that area, levitating enemies there (not effective against powerful enemies). \"Sa — Sakiri, can I eat this?\" \"Moron, next time ask before you eat!\" — —","m":["Press Ratio: 167.8% + 232.2%","Hold Ratio: 90.3% + 118.8% + 190.9%","CD: 16s","Press to Get Cycle Energy: 16","Hold to Get Cycle Energy: 23"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Feast of Gluttony","d":"No escaping this time! Kiroumaru spits out a large amount of Gravity Slurry from above, dealing 6 instances of Incantation DMG to an area. Applies strong gravity to hit enemies, pressing them heavily to the ground (not effective against Bosses). Prevents Suppressed enemies from moving for a period. Increases Team ATK (excluding Sakiri) based on Sakiri\u0027s Base ATK. No prey escapes before Kiroumaru has its fill.","m":["Gravity Slurry Ratio: 120% ×5 + 300%","CD: 20s","Costs Ultimate Energy: 120","Suppress Duration: 3s","ATK Bonus Ratio: 30%"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Squash!","d":"Let\u0027s see which unlucky soul is about to get squashed! Sakiri slams the enlarged Kiroumaru heavily onto the target, dealing 1 instance of Incantation DMG to an area. Kiroumaru, stop right there! Him? Did you just bump into something?","m":["DMG Ratio: 200%"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Can I Eat This? ","d":"Scorch Enhancement : Increases the DoT taken by the target by 25% for each type of DoT effect while in Scorch state, up to 100% . It\u0027s not time to start yet! Instead of swallowing whole — wouldn\u0027t it be better to add more ingredients? Can\u0027t let the fun pass!","m":[]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Impish Trick","d":"Reduces enemies\u0027 DEF by 10% for 20s after inflicting Airborne or Supress. Those on the naughty list — will be taken by ghosts… or perhaps eaten?","m":[]}],"how":"$undefined","pros":"Doesn’t need much field time. Can group and immobilize enemies. Passive DoT buffing. Universal support with DEF debuffs and ATK buffs.","cons":"Loses some of her potential outside of Scorch teams. Ult has high Energy cost.","teams":[{"n":"Scorch Team","m":["daffodil","baicang","adler"],"c":"This team focuses on cycling all 3 of the Incantation units with Daffodill to stack and maintain Scorch. Since Sakiri buffs DoT damage (including Scorch), she fits perfectly into this team.","r":""},{"n":"AoE Hexed Team","m":["nanally, mint","jiuyuan","baicang"],"c":"This team utilizes Sakiri as a buffer and enabler of the Hexed reaction. Since Hexed affects any Incantation or Anima damage, and lasts for 15 seconds, it is possible to keep up Hexed permanently in a team like this.","r":""}]},"Edgar":{"slug":"edgar","skills":[{"t":"Basic Attack","n":"Combat Practice","d":"Basic Attack: Combat Practice Applies what he learned in Lamplight Academy\u0027s physical education class to perform up to 5 consecutive attacks that deal Cosmos DMG . Basic Attack: Calculated Landing Press Basic Attack while airborne to plunge, dealing 1 instance of Cosmos DMG to an area upon impact. Increases DMG based on fall height, up to 100% . Critical Riposte: Crisis is Opportunity Triggers when using Combat Practice after a Critical Dodge. Charges toward the target and uses his backpack to unleash a Flow attack, dealing 1 instance of Cosmos DMG to an area and reducing Break. Edgar believes there must be a more humane way to contain them. Until that solution is found, he is forced to rely on rougher methods.","m":["1st Instance Ratio: 30.9%","2nd Instance Ratio: 62.7%","3rd Instance Ratio: 39% ×2","4th Instance Ratio: 83.3%","5th Instance Ratio: 69.8%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Wild Current","d":"Hold to enter a channeling state, continuously casting Current at the target, dealing Cosmos DMG and continuously healing the teammate with the lowest HP. The CD of Redirect Skill: Wild Current increases based on the duration of use. Healing is important work. Edgar realized that the rules he learned from games apply in real life as well.","m":["DMG Ratio: 80% ×7","Heal per Instance: 300 + 1.4% Max HP","Base CD: 16s","Additional CD per Instance: 1s","Cycle Energy: 37"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Finnegan\u0027s Wake","d":"Immerses in his own thoughts, unleashing a labyrinthine domain for 10 s. Deals 1 instance of AoE Cosmos DMG . Heals the current character over the domain\u0027s duration. Always curious, always questioning. Edgar often slips into deep thought without warning. Pulling him out of his complex musings is no easy task.","m":["DMG Ratio: 400%","Heal Amount: 350 + 1.1% Max HP","Healing Interval: 1s","Duration: 10s","CD: 20s"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Weight of Knowledge","d":"This bag is really heavy. Edgar charges toward the target and swings his bag with all his might, dealing 1 instance of Cosmos DMG to an area.","m":["DMG Ratio: 200%"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Gentle Edge","d":"Charge Enhancement : Grants 120 Ultimate Energy instantly when a character triggers Charge using a Support Skill. Disables Ultimate Energy gain from Vita Pistils when hitting Slowed targets afterward. Cooldown: 30 s. Like many geniuses, Edgar carries a quiet pride. Unlike most, his brilliance is gentle and understated, guiding him through every challenge he has faced.","m":[]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Unchanging Warmth","d":"Cast Redirect Skill Wild Current or Support Skill Weight of Knowledge to gain a Key of Truth , up to 3 keys. Each Key of Truth extends the duration of Ultimate: Finnegan\u0027s Vigil by 1 s. Whenever Edgar sees the warm lights of Eibon, comfort rises in his heart. In an ever-changing world, this warmth remains a constant.","m":[]}],"how":"Skia Hyper Skia · Zero (MC) · Haniel · Jiuyuan A Remora-Charge stealth team built around Skia\u0027s Fang Thrust stacking in Shadow Hound Gnaw mode, synergizing with Zero\u0027s Blossom and Jiuyuan for the Charge triple-cycle. Rotation Jiuyuan: Start with Jiuyuan and use her Ultimate (Final Reckoning) and Redirect Skill. Zero (MC): Switch to MC to trigger Blossom and use their Ultimate. Haniel: Switch to Haniel and use her Redirect Skill (Silent Moonlit Forest Guardian) and Ultimate (A Melody Named Haniel) to apply the ATK and Crit Damage buff (at R6). Skia: Swap to Skia to trigger Stain. Zero (MC): Quick-Swap from Skia to MC. Zero (MC): While on MC, use Redirect Skill. Skia: Swap to Skia to trigger Remora and Charge, then use his Redirect Skill (Shadow Hound Chase) followed by his Ultimate (The Pack). Skia: Remain in Shadow Hound Gnaw mode, pursuing Fang Thrust-marked enemies to detonate follow-up damage. Take time rebuilding energy and Cycle bar on Haniel. Repeat from the first step. Tips \u0026 Tricks Skia\u0027s Perfect Dodge needs to be timed precisely; otherwise he will sink into his shadow and still take the hit. When timed properly, his Dodge Counter has one of the longest i-frame windows in the game. Be careful when using Skia\u0027s Ultimate (The Pack) — make sure you are right next to the enemy. The attack is centered on Skia and can easily miss at range. Shadow Hound Chase costs no Stamina, allowing Skia to scale walls and buildings freely. Activating it before enemies detect him keeps them unaware during stealth sections.","pros":"Extremely low on-field time. Ultimate can have good uptime thanks to his passives.","cons":"Almost no utility. Doesn\u0027t bring anything unique. Healing will have low value for most players.","teams":[{"n":"F2P Charge Team","m":["skia","mint","zero"],"c":"Edgar provides support to this team via healing and allows any of his teammates to immediately get their Ultimate back when Charge is proceed.","r":""}]},"Hotori":{"slug":"hotori","skills":[{"t":"Basic Attack","n":"Misty Moon Style","d":"Basic Attack: Misty Moon Style Wields her weapon and performs up to 5 consecutive attacks, dealing Cosmos DMG . Basic Attack: Non-Closed Timepiece Displays a Non-Closed Timepiece when Hotori is switched in. Rotates its pointer slowly clockwise over time, accumulating energy. Caps the energy the Non-Closed Timepiece can accumulate at 120 . Basic Attack: Rippling Waves Hold Basic Attack in combat to trigger. Gracefully dashes forward and attacks, dealing 4 instances of Cosmos DMG to an area. Basic Attack: Crescent Wields the weapon mid-air and plunges, dealing 1 instance of Cosmos DMG to an area upon impact. Increases DMG based on fall height, up to 100% . Critical Riposte: Half Moment Triggers when using Misty Moon Style after a Critical Dodge. Raises the umbrella to counterattack opponents instantly, dealing 1 instance of Cosmos DMG and reducing Break. \"Finally, someone clueless comes along who actually wants to buy something from the shop, but if it wasn\u0027t for Daffodil refusing to budge, hmph — this month\u0027s sales wouldn\u0027t be a big fat zero.\"\"That little brat, didn\u0027t you see what kind of price he was trying to haggle? He\u0027s treating our Eibon like we\u0027re some charity case! I was being nice not calling Daff over to rough him up!\"","m":["1st Instance Ratio: 20%","2nd Instance Ratio: 35.3% + 4.4% ×2 + 72.2%","3rd Instance Ratio: 11.3% ×5","4th Instance Ratio: 14.2% ×2 + 66.6%","5th Instance Ratio: 24.3% + 45.1%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Present Replay","d":"Requires no cooldown for Present Replay. Allows Hotori to spend 60 Non-Closed Timepiece energy to cast Present Replay when energy is greater than 60 . Deals 7 instances of Cosmos DMG to an area. Records Support Skills and Redirect Skills used by allies for the next 5 s, appreciating up to 3 timings per use, with each character recorded at most once. Rewinds the Non-Closed Timepiece pointer continuously during use. Stops recording after the pointer rewinds a certain amount, and continues rewinding a fixed amount if recording completes early. Clears records when entering or leaving battle. Overwrites existing records when using Present Replay again. Observe and Witness","m":["DMG Ratio: 40% ×6 + 60.1%","Cycle Energy: 13"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"World\u0027s Tide","d":"Has no cooldown or Ultimate Energy cost for World\u0027s Tide. Allows Hotori to unleash World\u0027s Tide when Non-Closed Timepiece energy is fully charged, dealing 10 instances of Cosmos DMG to an area. Draws a katana from the umbrella handle and changes attack mode. Slows surrounding time to near standstill for a period, disabling character switching. Cleanses any received time control debuffs and grants immunity to time control debuffs during Time Stop. Replays all attacks recorded by Present Replay 1 time and clears the records if any exist. Rewinds the Non-Closed Timepiece pointer continuously during Time Stop. Builds combo stacks with Hotori\u0027s Katana attacks, increasing damage per hit. Deals Finisher DMG when combo stacks reach 10 . Ends time stop when the pointer rewinds completely or when Finisher DMG is dealt. Then — proceed toward the predetermined future.","m":["DMG Ratio: 17% ×6 + 130.3% + 44.3% + 261.6% ×2","Time Stop Duration: 10s","1st Katana Instance Ratio: 38.1%","2nd Katana Instance Ratio: 23.4% + 63.7%","3rd Katana Instance Ratio: 9.2% ×3 + 44.5%"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Shopkeeper\u0027s Authority","d":"Time to teach these rude guests some manners. Throws the umbrella, dealing 1 instance of Cosmos DMG to an area. For Hotori, this is merely a small display of her abilities, but difficult customers who threaten to complain will learn exactly what this humble little shop dares to impose such strict terms.","m":["DMG Ratio: 200%"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Ghost Orchid Crest","d":"Blossom Enhancement : Prevents Vita Bud attacks from pausing during Time Stop. At least when this proprietress, who can usually chatter on endlessly about every penny, finally quiets down and sits peacefully sipping wine while admiring the moon, you can still notice — she is an elegant and graceful person.","m":[]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"All Treasures Under Heaven","d":"Increases World\u0027s Tide\u0027s Finisher DMG Ratio by 100% . Cheers! Celebrate! Let\u0027s — let\u0027s celebrate again! My treasures — my precious treasures — they\u0027re all mine now! Deal — deal! Hehehe — hic — guard them well — for me — 2×2=4!","m":[]}],"how":"Hotori Blossom Hotori · Nanally · Zero (MC) · Jiuyuan A time-manipulation team centered on Hotori\u0027s Present Replay recording and replaying teammate Redirect Skills via her Ultimate (World\u0027s Tide), enabling massive burst windows for Nanally and Jiuyuan. Rotation Hotori: When Hotori has max energy, spend half to use her Redirect Skill (Present Replay) and begin recording teammate skills. Zero (MC): Within the 5-second recording window, use MC\u0027s Redirect Skill to fill the Cycle bar and Ultimate to proc Blossom. Jiuyuan: Switch to Jiuyuan and proc Blossom. Nanally: Switch to Nanally and use her Redirect Skill and Ultimate (Underboss). Nanally: Spend time on Nanally to use her Underboss follow-up attacks. Hotori: As Nanally\u0027s enhanced Basics run out, cast Hotori\u0027s Ultimate (World\u0027s Tide), which recasts everyone\u0027s recorded Redirect Skill, deals more damage from Nanally\u0027s Redirect Skill buff, and refills MC\u0027s Cycle bar. Before Hotori\u0027s Ultimate fills again, swap to Nanally for any Blossom procs to give her additional energy. Jiuyuan: Use Jiuyuan\u0027s Ultimate (Final Reckoning) and Redirect Skill. Repeat from the first step when Hotori has max energy again. Tips \u0026 Tricks If a Redirect Skill animation is too long and the 5-second recording window closes, the skill will not be recorded (e.g., Hathor\u0027s hold skill). Cancelling a Redirect Skill animation mid-way may also prevent it from registering. Some characters\u0027 skills are recorded at the start (Jiuyuan), while others only at the very end (Hathor). Hotori always replays the basic version of a recorded skill. Enhanced or hold versions (Daffodill, Hathor, Sakiri) are repeated in their normal form. Some character buffs require the character to be on-field to trigger (like Nanally\u0027s Crit DMG boost). Since Hotori repeats the skill rather than the character who cast it, those buffs will not activate during the repeat.","pros":"Her Ultimate has HUGE damage potential makes for a great damage window. Time Stop pauses the fight timer also, great for Beyond the Rails for example. Present Replay records your ally skills and fires them again for free inside Time Stop. She cleanses time control debuffs and grants immunity during Time Stop. The time stop also works in the Overworld.","cons":"You can’t switch out after using her Ultimate until Time Stop is over. The recording window for skills can be somewhat tight.","teams":[{"n":"Blossom Team","m":["jiuyuan","zero","nanally, mint"],"c":"This team focuses on generating as many Blossoms as possible through Esper Zero\u0027s Instant Cycle ability on their Skill and Hotori being able to repeat this skill during her Time Stop, while Jiuyuan and Nanally both have Blossom enhancements to amplify the damage from each proc.","r":""},{"n":"Charge Team","m":["jiuyuan, nanally, mint","zero","hathor, skia"],"c":"This team uses Hotori\u0027s skill replays to double up everyone\u0027s secondary effects, giving Hathor extra stacks, Jiuyuan extra bullets, and generating additional Esper Cycles, while also allowing for Charge procs to feed Hathor extra energy for more Ultimate uses.","r":"When Hotori has max energy, spend half to use her Skill and begin recording teammate skills. Within the 5-second window, you are aiming to: Use MC’s skill to fill the cycle bar and Ultimate to proc Speedy Hedgehog, then switch to Jiuyuan and proc Blossom, then switch to Hathor and use her skill. While waiting for the rest of Hotori’s energy to refill, we can use Jiuyuan’s ult, skill, and attachments. When available, swap back to Hotori and use her Ultimate. This Ultimate will recast everyone’s skill, providing 2 more feathers to Hathor and refilling MC’s Cycle bar again. You’ll want to immediately swap to Hathor and use her Ult and 3 enhanced skills to try to get them into the Speedy Hedgeho"}]},"Linko":{"slug":"linko","skills":[{"t":"Basic Attack","n":"Poltergeist CQC","d":"Basic Attack: Poltergeist CQC Casts Poltergeist CQC to perform up to 5 consecutive attacks, dealing Anima DMG . Builds up Modulation points with each hit. Casts Full-Frequency Pulse to consume Modulation points and enhance the triggered Synced Strike . Basic Attack: Spectral Smack Hold Basic Attack during Poltergeist CQC to make Linko strike the current target with both palms, dealing Anima DMG . Basic Attack: Spectral Entrance Press Basic Attack while airborne to plunge, dealing 1 instance of Anima DMG in an area upon impact. Increases DMG based on fall height by up to 100% . Basic Attack: Spectral Rush Sends Xiaozhen to ambush the target every 8s while Linko is off-field, causing Xiaozhen to attack once and inflict a Hit \u0027Em Here! mark. Critical Riposte: Ghosthand Counter Triggers when using Poltergeist CQC after a Critical Dodge. Charges toward the target, dealing 4 instances of Anima DMG in an area and building up Modulation. \"Xiaozhen, Xiaozhen, I\u0027ve got an idea… What if you threw punches like Ora Puncher? So fast, your fists would be nothing but afterimages!\" \"…Why bother? Wouldn\u0027t it be faster to knock them out with one good punch?\" \"You just don\u0027t get it! It\u0027s an art form!\"","m":["Poltergeist CQC: 1st Instance DMG Ratio: 49%","Poltergeist CQC: 2nd Instance DMG Ratio: 17% ×2","Poltergeist CQC: 3rd Instance DMG Ratio: 40%","Poltergeist CQC: 4th Instance DMG Ratio: 13% + 29% + 13% ×5 + 34%","Poltergeist CQC: 5th Instance DMG Ratio: 74%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Full-Frequency Pulse","d":"Channels Esper Ability upon casting Full-Frequency Pulse, bombarding the target with ghost energy to deal up to 4 instances of Anima DMG and calling Xiaozhen or an ally to perform a Synced Strike . Opens a selection wheel to choose Xiaozhen or an ally, then performs the selected character\u0027s Synced Strike , dealing DMG of the corresponding attribute. Grants this Synced Strike a DMG Bonus and consumes all accumulated Modulation, converting it into an additional DMG Bonus. Briefly pauses the battle timer while selecting the attacker and initiating the Synced Strike . Replaces an ally\u0027s position on the wheel with Xiaozhen if the ally is unable to act or is not on the team. Grants Xiaozhen\u0027s Synced Strike an additional DMG Bonus for each additional Xiaozhen on the wheel. Enable Auto-Cast Skills under \"Settings \u003e System Features\" to have the first ally in the team perform Synced Strike by default. \"Watch this! Our red-hot tag-team finisher…\" \"…Wait, kid. Did we even know that person?\" \"Didn\u0027t catch who it was, but the combo worked!\"","m":["Bombardment DMG Ratio: 17% + 13% + 23% + 44%","Modulation Point Cap: 100","Base Modulation DMG Bonus: 100%","Max Modulation DMG Bonus: 40%","DMG Bonus per Xiaozhen: 2%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Oversync","d":"Enters Overdrive upon casting Oversync, deploying a Resonance Field for a set duration and Syncing with up to 3 allies. Allows Redirect Skill to be pressed to call on Synced allies in sequence to perform Synced Strikes , up to 3 times. Deals 1 additional instance of Anima Area DMG when a Synced Strike is performed within Resonance Field. Ends Overdrive when its duration expires or when Oversync is pressed again, releasing an overloaded noise burst that deals multiple instances of Anima Area DMG and 1 instance of Anima Burst DMG to all enemies within Resonance Field. Increases this Anima Burst DMG based on the number of different debuffs on each target. Extends Resonance Field for a set duration after Overdrive ends. Counts Support Skills triggered by allies within Resonance Field as Synced Strikes , treats their DMG as Follow-up Attack DMG, and grants them the bonuses from Precision Tuning, Starlit Whispers, and The World Answers. Enable Auto-Cast Skills under \"Settings \u003e System Features\" to have allies perform Synced Strikes in sequence by default. No signal is ever truly lost. No one is ever beyond reach. No call goes unheard, and no distance can keep us apart… The airwaves will always bring us together, until meeting for the first time feels like finding each other again.","m":["Area DMG Ratio: 73%","Multi-Hit DMG Ratio: 57% ×6","Burst DMG Ratio: 735%","DMG Bonus per Debuff Type: 4%","Debuff DMG Bonus Cap: 20%"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Spectral Cross","d":"Strikes the target together with Xiaozhen, dealing 1 instance of Anima DMG in an area. Summons an ally to perform a Synced Strike by breaking a Hit \u0027Em Here! mark, casting Full-Frequency Pulse, or casting Oversync. Scales Synced Strike\u0027s DMG Ratio with Spectral Cross\u0027s skill level. \"What if some creep comes after me when you\u0027re not around…?\" \"Run. Those tiny legs of yours can really move.\" \"No way! Wait, I know. I\u0027ll hit them with the TV!\" \"No. Absolutely not. Under any circumstances.\"","m":[]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Weakness Radar","d":"Hexed Enhancement : Increases the base DMG of additional Follow-up Attacks from Hexed to 30% while Linko is on the team. Targets affected by Hexed take 10% more Follow-up Attack DMG. The faint static in that frequency felt like a crack no one else could see. How had it formed? And why did it refuse to heal? Sometimes, for just a moment, the thought left her quietly heartsick.","m":[]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Precision Tuning","d":"Reduces the target\u0027s Esper Ability Resistance corresponding to the attribute of the character who triggers Synced Strike by 8% for 12s . Resistance Reduction effects for different attributes can coexist on the same target. Effects of the same attribute inflicted by Synced Strike do not stack. Resets the duration when triggered again.","m":[]}],"how":"Linko is an Anima debuffer and Burst DPS that mainly functions as a Sub DPS. She doesn’t have a set rotation pre se, since she has low field time. Here’s some information about her kit and how it works so you can better understand how to play her and what to think about when using her on your teams! Basic Mechanics Modulation This is built up by using Basic attack or Linko’s Synced Strike. It buffs her skill damage, but not by such a big amount that it is worth basic attacking to stack this. Just let it accumulate passively as you use Synced Strikes and occasionally buff skill damage. Hit ‘Em Here Every 8 seconds in combat, Linko applies a ghostly mark debuff on the enemy. Whenever an ally uses their Redirect Skill, Linko will follow up with an attack that deals good damage and builds her Modulation bar. This debuff will refresh every 8 seconds, regardless of if the previous one was used or not. If Linko is on field during the 7th second, but switches off before the 8th second, it will still apply properly. It seems to tick the timer down even when she is on field, so long as she isn’t on field when the debuff is trying to be applied. Synced Strikes These are attacks that look like the support skill animation for a character, and they are triggered when using Linko’s Skill or Ultimate and scale with Linko’s Support Skill damage. The Synced Strikes triggered by Linko’s skill and Ultimate are the abilities that apply the 8% res shred to the enemies. Since this is based on character’s support skills, it is possible for it to miss on occasion for characters that have a melee-range support skill. Tips \u0026 Tricks When using Linko’s Skill, you can swap off of her during the animation, but before the selection wheel comes up, to automatically have her use Xiaozhen’s Synced Strike. Swap to Linko to use her Redirect Skill and then pick the main DPS to Sync Strike so that the uptime on their res down debuff is at 100% between Linko’s Ultimate and Redirect Skill usage. When paired with Iroi, her charged attack will still occur during the “time stop” from Linko’s Skill and Ultimate.","pros":"Has a unique mechanic called Synced Strikes, which functions similarly to a normal Support Skill but doesn\u0027t replace it or rely on the Cycle Gauge. It\u0027s the core of her kit and can work in any team regardless of attributes. Excellent Follow-Up Attack support, Synced Strike counts as Follow-Up Attack DMG. has a Hexed Enhancement which increases Follow Up Attack damage and causes Hexed targets to take additional Follow Up Attack DMG also Her Ultimate can sync with up to three teammates, with her Resonance Field turning their Support Skills into Follow-Up Attack DMG and enabling a large amount of Follow-Up Attacks and it deals a lot of damage. Can automatically trigger a Synced Strike when an ally uses a Redirect Skill on an enemy marked by Hit \u0027Em Here, allowing her to contribute even while off-field Can lower enemy Esper Ability Resistance based on the character triggering her Synced Stri","cons":"Needs to build up Modulation to get the most damage out of her Synced Strikes. Has some strong Awakenings, with A5 allowing her Synced Strikes to trigger Cycle Effects and A6 giving them Crit Rate and the Charge effect, all of this is locked behind her dupes and is not in her base kit.","teams":[{"n":"SubDPS","m":["sakiri","zankou, nanally","daffodil, lacrimosa"],"c":"Linko can be used as an Anima Sub DPS with a variety of Anima and Incantation damage dealers due to her excellent Hexed passive. She can also help break enemies more quickly and provides Esper resistance down.","r":""},{"n":"Main DPS","m":["sakiri","zero, hotori","iroi"],"c":"This is a team that can be played for fun with Linko if you don\u0027t have many other main DPS options. Her damage is good enough to be the main character on field if needed.","r":""}]},"Chiz":{"slug":"chiz","skills":[{"t":"Basic Attack","n":"Exiled Swordplay","d":"Basic Attack: Exiled Swordplay Swings the short staff to perform up to 5 consecutive attacks, dealing Cosmos DMG . Grants Grain on hit. Basic Attack: Barren Press Blighted Vale to throw Brown Sugar Boba to devour the target, dealing 2 instance of Cosmos DMG , granting a certain amount of Grain and Fons. Triggers up to once every 2.5s . Hold Blighted Vale during any instance of Exiled Swordplay attacks to create a branch attack, dealing 2 instance of Cosmos DMG and granting a certain amount of Grain and Fons. Grants bonus Fons if this skill defeats the target. Up to 250,000 Fons can be earned this way. Increasing the Tycoon Level to 25 raises the cap to 500,000 Fons. Grants 1 Fons per use once the daily cap is reached. After reaching the total limit, no more Fons can be obtained this way. Basic Attack: Bountiful Grain Press Basic Attack while airborne to plunge, dealing 1 instance of Cosmos DMG to an area upon impact, while granting a certain amount of Grain . Increases DMG based on fall height, up to 100% . Critical Riposte: Minsky Moment Triggers when pressing Basic Attack after a Critical Dodge. Leaps to evade and swings the staff, sending Brown Sugar Boba crashing into the target, dealing 1 instance of Cosmos DMG , reducing Break, and granting Grain . Jade for good times, grain for lean times.","m":["1st Instance Ratio: 34.5%","2nd Instance Ratio: 17.1% ×3","3rd Instance Ratio: 56%","4th Instance Ratio: 20.9% ×5","5th Instance Ratio: 39.7% ×2"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Pink Paws Priority Principle","d":"The more, the merrier; the more, the better. Stacks Redirect Skill attempts, up to 3 stacks Press Redirect Skill to consume 1 stack and cast No Grain, dealing Cosmos DMG once. Press Redirect Skill consecutively to consume stacks and cast No Grain, Half Grain, and Full Grain in order, up to 3 times in a row. Press to cast Pink Paws Priority Principle while in the Surplus state, dealing bonus Cosmos DMG based on available Grains using Redirect Skills. Cannot Crit. Hold Redirect Skill to consume 2 skill charges and cast No Grain and Half Grain. Continuously consumes Grains while Half Grain is active, dealing consecutive bonus Cosmos DMG based on available Grains. Cannot Crit. Consumes all available Grains (including all Grain Loans from the Debt state) when Half Grain ends. Press Redirect Skill again to consume 1 stack and end Half Grain early, allowing Full Grain to be cast without consuming Grains . Hold Redirect Skill to consume 3 stacks and use all available Grains (including all Grain Loans from the Debt state). Casts No Grain, Half Grain, and Full Grain in order. Hold to Cast Pink Paws Priority Principle while Surplus is active, dealing bonus Cosmos DMG with No Grain based on remaining Grains . Cannot Crit. Frontispiece of the Pink Paws Bank Employee Handbook: In tribute to the great Lord Ladon.","m":["DMG Ratio of No Grain: 19% + 40%","Hit DMG Ratio of Half Grain: 53.2% ×2","Per Instance DMG Ratio of Half Grain: 25%","DMG Ratio of Full Grain: 28.3% + 41.8% ×3","Bonus DMG per Grain: 3"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Zero-Sum Game","d":"No turning back, max the leverage. Throws Brown Sugar Boba to strike, dealing AoE Cosmos DMG once and entering Grain Market for 7s . During this time, the first Grain Settlement DMG is guaranteed to Crit. Converts all remaining Grain Loans into Grains and enters the Surplus state after casting Zero-Sum Game. Invests all Grains into the Grain Market. Afterward, press Pink Paws Priority Principle to gain Grains based on current Grain Price fluctuations during Grain Settlement . Hold Pink Paws Priority Principle to trigger Grain Settlement once based on the Grain Price on first activation. Leaves the Grain Market and prioritizes repaying Grain Loans with all available Grains when Grain Market duration ends. Grants access to the Grain Market while in Debt state and holding any Grain Loans . I will be the only one to win this battle.","m":["DMG Ratio: 44.6% ×4 + 44.7% + 277.1%","Grain Market Duration: 7s","Costs Ultimate Energy: 100","CD: 15s"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Temporary Entry","d":"Hope I can m-make it in time… Brown Sugar Boba carries Chiz and crashes into the target, dealing 1 instance of Cosmos DMG .","m":["DMG Ratio: 200%"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Hanahaki Disease","d":"Charge Enhancement : Grants active characters 4 additional Charge. Longing — it\u0027s a white bird rising from a wound. If only you could see.","m":[]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Hoarding","d":"Increases Chiz\u0027s Charge Efficiency by 20% while on the field. The past is a bottomless ravine. No matter how many stones you throw, not a single echo ever returns.","m":[]}],"how":"Chiz Hyper Chiz · Zero (MC) · Jiuyuan · Hathor A Cosmos, Anima, and Lakshana Charge team built around maximising Chiz\u0027s Grain Market mechanic and Zero-Sum Game Ultimate, supported by Jiuyuan\u0027s Blossom procs and Hathor\u0027s Ultimate. Rotation Zero (MC): Start with MC using their Redirect Skill. Chiz: Swap to Chiz to use her Ultimate (Zero-Sum Game) and enter the Surplus State. Chiz: Press the 1st Redirect Skill button when the Grain Market bar is in the positive. (The 2nd and 3rd Redirect Skills can be pressed at -5% or better.) Chiz: After using all of Chiz\u0027s Redirect Skills, swap to Jiuyuan. Jiuyuan: Use Jiuyuan\u0027s Ultimate (Final Reckoning) and Redirect Skill. By now MC\u0027s Redirect Skill should be nearly off cooldown. Zero (MC): Swap to MC, then swap from MC to Jiuyuan to trigger a Blossom, then go back to MC. Zero (MC): Use MC\u0027s Redirect Skill and Ultimate, then swap to Hathor to trigger Charge. Hathor: If Hathor has enough feathers (Express Delivery Power stacks), use her Ultimate (Rider Express) immediately; otherwise use her Redirect Skill (Aerial Command) first. Hathor: Use her enhanced Redirect Skill combo (Cyclone Strike) if available. Chiz: Swap to Chiz to use 2 charges of her Redirect Skill while waiting for Charge to tick up her Ultimate energy. Repeat from the first step. Tips \u0026 Tricks If you are lucky with the Grain Market, you can use four Redirect Skills within the 7-second Surplus window. If the Grain Market starts unfavorably, swap to another character and use a quick Redirect Skill or Support Skill while waiting to get into the positive. Chiz\u0027s held 2nd Redirect Skill (Half Grain) deals significant additional damage and can be used when a boss is nearing death and you do not need to replenish the Grain it costs.","pros":"Strong free main DPS, including full copies being obtainable without spending High damage ceiling when Grain is managed properly Can stay active while swapping characters during her multi-cast Redirect Skill sequence Awakening and Resonance improve both Grain generation and damage conversion. Deals a lot of damage. Shop management buffs.","cons":"Mechanically complex, especially around Grain timing and Grain Market optimization. A bit of a selfish DPS.","teams":[{"n":"Charge Team","m":["jiuyuan, nanally, mint","hathor, skia","zero, hotori"],"c":"This team utilizes Charge to spread the Ultimate energy across multiple teammates for high Ultimate uptime on everyone.","r":""},{"n":"Chiz Hypercarry Team","m":["jiuyuan, nanally, mint","hathor, skia","haniel, sakiri"],"c":"This team focuses on setting up Haniel’s buffs for Chiz’s on field time and using Charge to refill Chiz and the buffers Ultimate. It also happens to excel in AoE damage just by the nature of all of the characters on the team having great AoE.","r":""}]},"Nanally":{"slug":"nanally","skills":[{"t":"Basic Attack","n":"Colucci Secret Skill","d":"Basic Attack: Colucci Secret Skill Bares her fangs and brandishes her claws, performing up to 5 consecutive attacks, dealing Anima DMG . Dodging does not interrupt the combo. Basic Attack: Heavy Hitter! Triggers by holding Basic Attack. Performs up to 3 powerful attacks, dealing Anima DMG . Chains after Critical Riposte and the 1st, 2nd, 3rd, and 5th attacks of Colucci Secret Skill. Dodging does not interrupt the combo. Basic Attack: Colucci Secret Gundo Enters aim mode, dealing 1 instance of single-target Anima DMG to the enemy in the crosshair. Basic Attack: Grand Entrance! Swings her claws in the air and plunges, dealing 1 instance of Anima DMG to an area upon impact. Increases DMG based on fall height, up to 100% . Critical Riposte: Can\u0027t Touch This! Triggers when using Colucci Secret Skill after a Critical Dodge. Charges toward the target at full speed, planting one hand on the ground, delivering a roundhouse kick that deals 1 instance of Anima DMG to an area, and reducing Break. Said to be a secret combat technique passed down in the Colucci, though it clearly incorporates many street-fighting elements from Hethereau.","m":["1st Instance Ratio: 29.6%","2nd Instance Ratio: 38.8%","3rd Instance Ratio: 12.2% + 21% + 127.1%","4th Instance Ratio: 6.9% × 7","5th Instance Ratio: 77.2% + 77.4%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Colucci Howling Technique","d":"Hehe, surprise time! Deals 5 instances of Anima DMG to surrounding enemies and wraps herself in Anima Esper Ability, gaining the Ichi-daime\u0027s Authority effect. Lasts 12 s or until Nanally is switched out. Ends Ichi-daime\u0027s Authority early when recast. Mint tried to learn this move from Nanally, but the moment she saw that Nanally\u0027s hair went rough, curved, split, and knotted, she gave up the idea. Adler is not with her in the Bureau of Anomaly Control to take care of her hair, after all.","m":["Area DMG Ratio: 100% ×5","CD: 16s","Cycle Energy: 11","Crit DMG Increase: 30%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Colucci Ultimate Technique","d":"I\u0027m way stronger than them! Deals 7 instances of Anima DMG immediately to surrounding enemies and summons Underboss to fight alongside her. Creates a small pull effect on surrounding enemies with Nanally\u0027s attacks while Underboss is active, and coordinates with all of Nanally\u0027s attacks to launch strikes, dealing Anima DMG that also counts as follow-up attack damage. \"A proper gang leader will give her goons some room to shine in the spotlight — I can\u0027t fight without my goons?! Ahem, are you having doubts about my strength?\"","m":["Area DMG Ratio: 293.1% + 42.3% ×5 + 495.4%","Underboss Basic Attack: 1st Instance DMG Ratio: 25%","Underboss Basic Attack: 2nd Instance DMG Ratio: 22%","Underboss Basic Attack: 3rd Instance DMG Ratio: 42.5% + 40","Underboss Basic Attack: 4th Instance DMG Ratio: 31.7% * 3"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Justice from Above","d":"Time to get serious! Charges with a spinning motion, delivering a kick and dealing 1 instance of Anima DMG to an area. Got a problem? Come find Nanally — I\u0027ve got you covered!","m":["DMG Ratio: 200%"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"More Than Passionate","d":"Blossom Enhancement : Fires 10 Vita Pistils with each Vita Bud, reducing the interval between each shot to 1 s. The First Rule of Gang Wars: \"Watch your back.\"","m":[]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Fair Duel","d":"Applies 1 follow-up attack to a single enemy, dealing Anima DMG of 60% ATK whenever any character in the team deals 1 instance of Esper Cycle DMG to an enemy while in Ichi-daime\u0027s Authority state. DMG Ratio scales with Basic Attack skill level, reaching 129.5% at Lvl 11. Triggers once every 2s . \"Hey, hey, hey! The duel\u0027s already started! Running soooo far away… Chickening out, huh?\"","m":[]}],"how":"Nanally Hyper Nanally · Zero (MC) · Jiuyuan · Sakiri A Blossom-focused team built around Nanally\u0027s Underboss follow-up attacks and Crit Damage buff, combining Hexed reactions from Sakiri with Blossom procs from Jiuyuan and Zero. Rotation Jiuyuan: Start on Jiuyuan, then switch to MC to proc Blossom. Zero (MC): Use MC\u0027s Redirect Skill and Ultimate, then switch to Sakiri. Sakiri: Use her Ultimate and Redirect Skill (Devour Whole) to buff the team, then swap to Jiuyuan. This procs Hexed and sets up Nanally. Jiuyuan: Use her Ultimate (Final Reckoning) and Redirect Skill, then swap to Nanally. Nanally: Use her Redirect Skill into her Ultimate (Underboss), then perform her enhanced Basic Attack combo. Burst rotation is now complete. Two Reaction procs remain: one for Nanally into an Incantation teammate, and one for MC into an Anima teammate. Use Blossom freely to gain extra damage. Spend time building Ultimate energy for Nanally and Sakiri. Save the other Hexed proc for the second rotation. Complete the second rotation; by the end, another Support Skill should be available to keep Hexed ongoing. Repeat from the first step. Tips \u0026 Tricks Using Nanally\u0027s Redirect Skill before her Ultimate is preferred in almost every situation due to the Crit Damage buff it provides. The only exception is if you are using Raging Flames. Playing Nanally as the main on-field unit, landing Dodge Counters or swapping into her, can help with her Ultimate energy generation. To maximize Underboss and her enhanced Basic Attacks, perform the full 5-hit Basic Attack string then the 3-hit Charged Attack string. You will exhaust Underboss charges exactly at this point without any Awakenings.","pros":"Both Ichi-Daime\u0027s Authority and Underboss stacking together means her damage will be very high once both are active. Boosts Blossom output just by running her normal rotation, so she\u0027s contributing to the whole team. Straightforward rotation that isn\u0027t hard to pick up Walks on walls in the overworld which is genuinely useful for exploration. + Shop Management buffs (and can bonk customers!)","cons":"Wants a lot of uninterrupted field time and loses a significant chunk of her burst window the moment she gets hit. Ichi-Daime\u0027s Authority doesn\u0027t persist when you switch out, so if you\u0027re forced off field you\u0027re rebuilding from scratch.","teams":[{"n":"Blossom Team","m":["jiuyuan","zero","hotori, sakiri, haniel"],"c":"This team focuses on generating as many Blossoms as possible through MC\u0027s Instant Cycle ability on their Skill and Hotori being able to repeat this during her Time Stop. Nanally has pretty high field time to take advantage of that synergy, as no one else on this team takes much field time. For those missing Hotori, other options like Haniel or Sakiri can provide damage boosts.","r":""},{"n":"Hexed Team","m":["sakiri","jiuyuan, mint","adler"],"c":"Nanally will be the main damage dealer in this team, but everyone can take advantage of the Hexed reaction here. With 2 characters of each attribute it is possible to maintain Hexed 100% of the time.","r":"The goal is to have buffs and Hexed up when doing Nanally’s on-field damage. If starting with max resources, we would want to start on Jiuyuan and switch into Adler. Then we use Adler’s skill and ultimate then switch off to Sakiri. After Sakiri’s Ult and skill have buffed the team, we can swap to Jiuyuan for her Ult and Skill. Then we go to Nanally and use her skill into ult and enhanced basic attack combo. From this point the burst rotation is over, but we still have the Hexed procs for Nanally into an Incantation teammate and Adler into an Anima teammate as well. One of these can be used freely to gain extra damage while getting ult energy for Nanally and Sakiri, and the other should be sa"}]},"Aurelia":{"slug":"aurelia","skills":[{"t":"Basic Attack","n":"Cappella","d":"Basic Attack: Legato Sing smoothly and naturally! Wields her weapon and performs up to 4 consecutive attacks, dealing Psyche DMG . Basic Attack: Staccato Sing loudly and fully! Hold Dodge while moving to ride a jellyfish, sprinting at high speed for the duration. Generates a jellyfish blast at intervals when targets are nearby, dealing Psyche DMG . Performs a special Dodge in this state, and \"Critical Riposte: Syncopation\" automatically fires four jellyfish blasts. Ends automatically when stamina drops below a certain amount. Basic Attack: Portamento Sing clearly and beautifully! Wields the weapon mid-air and plunges, dealing 1 instance of Psyche DMG to an area upon impact. Increases DMG based on fall height, up to 100% . Critical Riposte: Syncopation Triggers when casting Legato after a Critical Dodge. Think you can handle my rhythm? Wields her weapon to deal 1 instance of Psyche DMG to an area and reduces Break. Vocal technique is key for any conductor, so I keep practicing. Engage the core, relax the jaw, let the sound flow from the back of my head and out through my brow... \"Ah—ah—\" ...Why does it feel like even my own voice is slipping away?","m":["1st Instance DMG Ratio: 34.7%","2nd Instance DMG Ratio: 63%","3rd Instance Projectile DMG Ratio: 30% ×3","4th Instance DMG Ratio: 9.9% ×4","Plunge Attack DMG Ratio: 130%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Cadenza Aria","d":"Transform the everyday into a rainbow melody and let it roar across the skyline. Deals 1 instance of AoE Psyche DMG and enters the Cadenza state for 12 s. If she hadn\u0027t joined the Tamamachi Street Resident Association, Aurelia might have ended up as an administrator on Cadenza Street instead. In the end, perhaps it\u0027s all just a matter of fate.","m":["DMG Ratio: 100%","Projectile Enhancement Ratio: 70%","Buff Duration: 12s","Cooldown: 15s","Cycle Energy: 11"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Canzon Chorus","d":"Let\u0027s play the next verse together. Gathers nearby jellyfish, dealing 6 instances of AoE Psyche DMG and slightly pulling targets together. Whether it was the school choir or that short-lived, chaotic band, these were Aurelia\u0027s most cherished memories. Even a brilliant solo would feel far too lonely.","m":["DMG Ratio: 89% ×5 + 55.2%","Cooldown: 15s","Costs Ultimate Energy: 120"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Dissonance","d":"True command means never mistaking the timing. Commands the jellyfish to strike, dealing 1 instance of AoE Psyche DMG on hit.","m":["DMG Ratio: 200%"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Harmonics","d":"Nova Enhancement: Deals 3 instances of Psyche DMG to the target after their Nova status ends, each equal to 50% of ATK. How do you prove that sound is a wave? Toss a stone into water and see the ripples spread; toss a stone at someone, and you\u0027ll hear wave after wave of noise. \"...Am I supposed to laugh?\" \"Aurelia\u0027s jokes aren\u0027t funny at all—\" \"No way! People used to eat that up... you kids just have your humor standards way too high.\"","m":[]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Crescendo","d":"Increases Aurelia\u0027s ATK by 1% for 5s when a jellyfish blast hits a target, up to 10 stacks. Strong... stronger... Super Sound... Ultimate Sound! Want it even louder? Then the drummer will just have to throw themselves into the drum headfirst!","m":[]}],"how":"Aurelia Hyper Aurelia · Hathor · Jiuyuan · Zero (MC) A Stain-Charge team built around Aurelia\u0027s Critical Dodge Riposte (Syncopation) mechanic, enabled by Hathor\u0027s Remora and Jiuyuan\u0027s Blossom procs. Rotation Jiuyuan: Start with Jiuyuan and use her Ultimate (Final Reckoning) and Redirect Skill. Zero (MC): Swap to MC and use their Ultimate and Redirect Skill. Hathor: Swap to Hathor to trigger Remora and hold-charge her Redirect Skill (Aerial Command) to gain feathers. Aurelia: Swap to Aurelia and proc Stain, then use her Redirect Skill and Ultimate. Hathor: Swap back to Hathor to use her Ultimate (Rider Express) and 3 enhanced Redirect Skills (Cyclone Strike). Aurelia: During the 3rd Cyclone Strike, swap back to Aurelia and use Basic Attacks while looking for opportunities to Perfect Dodge. Setup Ultimate energy on Hathor and MC for the next rotation. Repeat from the first step. Tips \u0026 Tricks As Aurelia, your main focus is Perfect Dodging, since a large portion of her damage comes from Critical Dodge Riposte (Syncopation). This is buffed further when her Redirect Skill is active. There is no audio cue for her Perfect Dodge, but the visual effect will appear, or she will fire 4 jellyfish blasts (Critical Dodge Riposte: Syncopation).","pros":"High-mobility playstyle built around Critical Riposte and Syncopation, where dodging triggers burst damage without needing much setup. Jellyfish Blast keeps firing on its own, dodges trigger extra blasts, and Harmonics steadily ramps damage as you play. As an A-rank, you can get all of her awakenings, getting better crits, longer Cadenza uptime, and stronger ultimate damage. Shop management buffs, and bro she has a jellyfish.","cons":"Very on-field dependent, so she likely competes heavily for field time and may not fit quick-swap teams well. Requires good stamina management and can feel a bit clunky at times if you are not used to her playstyle, due to the delay in dealing damage before she enters her higher movement speed mode. Give me blasts, give me power, but if you give me a sidewalk, I won’t walk on it. (She can’t climb either)","teams":[{"n":"Nova Team","m":["daffodil","haniel","fadia"],"c":"This team focuses on causing the Nova reaction as often as possible to utilize Fadia’s HP drain, Haniel’s Attack drain, and Aurelia’s extra Nova damage.","r":""},{"n":"Hypercarry Aurelia","m":["hathor, skia","zero, hotori","jiuyuan, nanally, mint"],"c":"This team utilizes the Charge reaction to battery Aurelia and Hathor’s Ultimates. It performs well in AoE just by the nature of the characters that are in the team.","r":""}]},"Iroi":{"slug":"iroi","skills":[{"t":"Basic Attack","n":"Collaboration ","d":"Basic Attack: Collaboration Summons lambs to perform up to 5 consecutive attacks, dealing Anima DMG . Builds up Imagination when attacks hit. Basic Attack: Daydream Hold Basic Attack to charge up, consuming Imagination based on the charge duration to unleash up to 3 instances of Daydream, dealing Anima DMG . Hold Basic Attack during Reflexive Response, Bang!, Future Self Continuity, and 3.8-Billion-Year Mirage, consuming Imagination to unleash the 3rd instance of Daydream, dealing Anima DMG . Basic Attack: Lucid Dream Hold Basic Attack again after Iroi uses Basic Attack: Daydream to consume Imagination , summoning Morpheus to unleash sustained fire that deals Anima DMG . Basic Attack: Wakey-Wakey Press Basic Attack while airborne to plunge, dealing 1 instance of Anima DMG to an area upon impact. Increases DMG based on fall height by up to 100% . Builds up Imagination on hit. Reflexive Response Triggers when using Basic Attack: Collaboration after a Critical Dodge. Throws Morpheus at the target, dealing 1 instance of Anima DMG and reducing Break. Builds up Imagination on hit. …Bzz—bzz bzz—bzz bzz bzz…","m":["Collaboration: 1st Instance DMG Ratio \u0026 Builds up Imagination: 76%, 2","Collaboration: 2nd Instance DMG Ratio \u0026 Builds up Imagination: 15.9% ×3, 3","Collaboration: 3rd Instance DMG Ratio \u0026 Builds up Imagination: 10.3% ×8, 3","Collaboration: 4th Instance DMG Ratio \u0026 Builds up Imagination: 70.2%, 4","Collaboration: 5th Instance DMG Ratio \u0026 Builds up Imagination: 25.8% ×3, 8"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Future Self Continuity ","d":"Self-Identity Extension Press to activate. Summons lambs to heal all team members once and grant them an ATK bonus based on Iroi’s Base ATK. Summons three lambs to attack respectively, dealing Anima DMG and pulling in nearby enemies. Using this skill builds up Imagination . Future Self Continuity Hold to activate. Creates dreamlike illusions during battle, causing 3 allies to enter the Regression state and assist in battle. Regression is automatically removed after leaving combat. Passive While Iroi is on the team and in combat, any ally who falls enters the Regression state. Builds up Imagination when any fallen ally enters the Regression state. I have to stay awake the night before my birthday. I believe that if I fall asleep, someone will come for the old me and leave a newly grown me in its place.","m":["Redirect Skill: Three Lambs\u0027 Attack Ratio: 150% + 17.9% ×7 + 125%","Bonus Ratio Based on Iroi\u0027s Base ATK: 20%","ATK Bonus Duration: 20s","Healing Ratio: 94.3%","Regression: Morpheus - Sweet Dreams Base ATK Ratio: 55.5%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"3.8-Billion-Year Mirage ","d":"Return to the first dream. Opens the gate to a dream and triggers different effects based on the amount of Imagination built up. If Imagination has not reached the required threshold: Iroi opens the Dream of the Horned Gate, continuously healing all allies. If Imagination has reached the required threshold: Iroi opens the Dream of the Ivory Gate, continuously healing all allies and dealing Anima DMG to enemies inside the dream. During this time, press and hold the avatar of a team member in the Regression state to temporarily revive them and restore a portion of their HP. This effect can revive up to 1 character during each dream. The dream continuously consumes Imagination . When Imagination is depleted, the dream ends, and the revived character returns to the Regression state. While the dream is active, Imagination cannot be built up, but casting Daydream and Lucid Dream do not consume Imagination . I heard the bell at both ends of the dream: once at the beginning, once at the end. But the bell only rang once. From hydrothermal vents in the deep sea to skyscrapers on land, that awful chime has followed everything. Oh my, it\u0027s been ringing for 3.8 billion years.","m":["Post-Cast Healing Ratio: 141.3%","Continuous Healing Ratio: 31.4%","Post-Cast DMG Ratio: 300%","DoT Ratio: 25%","Imagination Limit: 100"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Bang! ","d":"Just in time! Picks up Morpheus and strikes forward, dealing 1 instance of Anima DMG , healing all team members, and building up Imagination . Would you believe me if I said this is the sound of the Big Bang?","m":["DMG Ratio: 200%","Healing Ratio: 60%"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Mirror Image ","d":"Blossom Enhancement : Generates a Vita Bud Copy when the current Vita Bud has existed for 3s . This copy cannot duplicate and does not count toward the Vita Bud limit. The copy produces 20 Copied Vita Pistils. Every 0.5s , one Copied Vita Pistil flies toward a target within range and explodes, dealing 37.5% of the original Vita Pistil\u0027s DMG. Sometimes, my shadow gets there before I do.","m":[]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Sympathetic Nerves ","d":"Grants all team members an additional 5% DEF Ignore for 20s when performing healing. My body lives on faithfully, covered in scars and never saying a word.","m":[]}],"how":"Iroi is an Anima support and healer that can function as a main DPS in an emergency, or for fun. She doesn’t have a set rotation, since she is mainly a support character. Here’s some information about her kit and how it works so you can better understand how to play her and what to think about when using her on your teams! Support Iroi When a teammate falls in battle, they automatically turn into a sheep Using Iroi\u0027s Ultimate deals “DoT” damage and drains her Imagination (caps at 12.5 seconds) This is not technically DoT damage, and instead is a pulse from the character during Iroi’s ultimate duration. As such, it does not contribute to Sakiri’s passive for extra damage dealt from DoT. Team gets continuous healing while this is active Her Blossom effect lasts a total of 13 seconds (3 seconds after the base blossom, her copied blossom appears and lasts 10s) Iroi can heal the entire team from her Redirect Skill, Support Skill, and Ultimate. DPS Iroi Sheep Transformation Iroi\u0027s Hold Skill turns the whole team into sheep Hold the character’s respective swap button for whichever teammate you want to Unsheep The Unsheep effect sticks around until Iroi\u0027s Imagination runs dry (roughly 12 seconds max) You\u0027re able to Unsheep a teammate even if they\u0027ve fallen, since all fallen allies become sheep Esper Cycling Sheep seem to inherit Iroi\u0027s stats when dealing damage Iroi can Esper Cycle with sheep, even though she doesn\u0027t actually swap off-field, this is based on Iroi’s stats. Esper Cycling with sheep doesn\u0027t pull from the original character\u0027s Esper Cycle stat Only Iroi can Esper Cycle with sheep, unsheeped characters can\u0027t do it themselves Iroi can also Esper Cycle with an Unsheeped character Sheeped Characters Character’s reaction passives still work, while they are turned into sheep. Eg. Jiuyuan\u0027s double blossom passive will still trigger if you proc a Blossom Sheepified characters still generate Energy and keep their mechanics active (Hathor Feathers, Hotori\u0027s time energy, etc.)","pros":"Good healing; can keep the whole team healthy with her Redirect, Ult, and swap heal. Gives team buffs with DEF shred and ATK% boost. Can group enemies together with her Redirect Skill. Does decent damage while healing, especially with her Ult. Has good range and feels smooth to play.","cons":"Easy to mess up with her Redirect long-press, which can weaken your team for the whole fight. Needs to stay on the field a bit to charge her Ult.","teams":[{"n":"Iroi Charge Support","m":["iroi","hathor","zero"],"c":"This team structure is where Iroi shines the most, because her kit does well with being on field for a short amount of time. You will mainly just Ult and Skill on her, and setup the main DPS. With her passive, her Blossoms will tick for 13s and Hathor\u0027s Remora debuff lasts for 12s so the goal is to setup Blossom first, then Remora, and on-field the main DPS to get the most out of Charge.","r":""},{"n":"Iroi Blossom","m":["nanally","jiuyuan","zero, hotori"],"c":"Since Iroi\u0027s Blossom is roughly 1.5x the damage of a base Blossom, she benefits more from Jiuyuan in this team than Nanally. Even still, Nanally would be the main on-field DPS while waiting for Hotori\u0027s energy or the rest of the team\u0027s cooldowns.","r":""},{"n":"Iroi Main DPS","m":["sakiri","jiuyuan","zero, hotori"],"c":"Sheepify your allies and have Iroi take the wheel. At A0, this is mostly a meme team but becomes a bit more viable with her A4 and A6.","r":""}]},"Baicang":{"slug":"baicang","skills":[{"t":"Basic Attack","n":"Walk the Talk","d":"Basic Attack: Walk the Talk Uses martial arts to perform up to 5 consecutive attacks, dealing Incantation DMG . Basic Attack: Formless Words Hold Basic Attack to trigger Formless Words after the 1 st and 2 nd hits of Walk the Talk. Release the stick and hold Dodge to trigger Formless Words during battle. Fires 3 incantation commands horizontally. After a brief delay, the commands detonate, with each dealing 1 instance of Incantation DMG to an area. Basic Attack: Unrestrained Words Hold Basic Attack to trigger Unrestrained Words after the 3 rd hit of Walk the Talk. Hold down the stick and hold Dodge to trigger Unrestrained Words during battle. Fires 3 incantation commands vertically. After a brief delay, the commands detonate, with each dealing 1 instance of Incantation DMG to an area. Basic Attack: In the Wind Leaps in the wind and strikes, dealing 1 instance of Incantation DMG to an area upon impact. Increases DMG based on fall height, up to 100% . Critical Riposte: Truth Exposed Triggers when casting Walk the Talk after a Critical Dodge. Performs a knee strike on the target, dealing 1 instance of Incantation DMG to an area, reducing their Break. Generates 1 Bless word on the target when hit. Basic Attack: Shadow Follows Generates a Power Word Bless on the enemy for every 3 Walk the Talk hits. This word lasts for 15 s, and a maximum of 3 can be generated. Consumes 3% of Baicang\u0027s current HP whenever any Power Word is summoned. When Baicang\u0027s HP is below 50% , the amount consumed is halved. Just some really basic moves. Day after day of training under family discipline since childhood, the young boy\u0027s arms have become strong and broad.","m":["1st Instance Ratio: 47.5%","2nd Instance Ratio: 42.3%","3rd Instance Ratio: 119%","4th Instance Ratio: 25.1% ×3","5th Instance Ratio: 86.3%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Generous Guidance","d":"Heart of Heaven and Earth Words and text emerge from the ley lines, converge at the target location, and unleash an attack. Silenced Thought Press Redirect Skill after triggering a dodge. Attacks a single target, dealing Incantation DMG to them on hit. Generates 1 Power Word Silence on the target when attacks hit. Such Crime Press Redirect Skill after triggering Formless Words or Unrestrained Words. Expanded the damage range, dealing AoE Incantation DMG on hit. Generates 1 Power Word Objurgate on the ground near the target when attacks hit. Every strike carries genuine intent. The voice once found, the home once briefly held, keeping memories of the departed close to heart. Smile! For now he has the power to protect.","m":["\"Heart of Heaven and Earth\" DMG Ratio: 120%","Silenced Thought Missile DMG Ratio: 100% ×3","Silenced Thought Explosion DMG Ratio: 120%","\"Such Crime\" DMG Ratio: 280%","\"Heart of Heaven and Earth\" CD: 14s"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Judgment of Autumn","d":"Look up, and fall into the polar abyss. Releases a domain and enters Power Word state, dealing Incantation DMG over time to targets. Executes the target when their HP is below 10% (Boss HP below 5% ). Becomes immune to 1 fatal hit temporarily during Judgment of Autumn and records its value. Ends the domain automatically 3 s after triggering the immunity effect and takes the recorded damage slowly over 10 s after ending. Deals high single-target damage within the domain when Silence is triggered; Deals AoE DMG when Objurgate is triggered; Deals damage to a single target and restores 5% of Baicang\u0027s Max HP when Bless is triggered. No one understands the power of words themselves better than Baicang. Until the very last moment, no one knows whether those waveforms taking shape in the air represent curses or blessings. Perhaps—only by glimpsing into the heart can one truly discern.","m":["Judgment of Autumn Expansion DMG Ratio: 400%","Judgment of Autumn DoT DMG Ratio: 40%","Judgment of Autumn Duration: 12s","DoT Interval: 2s","Silence DMG Ratio: 300%"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Break Time Over","d":"Witness the power that words bestow. Charges briefly and writes incantation commands, targeting enemies and dealing 1 instance of Incantation DMG to an area. Generates 1 Power Word Silence on target when attacks hit.","m":["DMG Ratio: 200%"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Moderate Mischief","d":"Scorch Enhancement : Inflicts another instance of Scorch with the same effect as the existing one when a Power Word is generated on a target affected by Scorch. Sigh… break time\u0027s over again. Now then, let\u0027s wrap this up quickly, shall we?","m":[]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Moderate Working","d":"Increases Baicang\u0027s ATK by 20% . Launches coordinate attacks with the allies when there are ETD- 4 members in the Team. In combat, switching to Baicang while Skia is in stealth to immediately attack with Baicang and generate 1 Power Word Silence on target. Cooldown: 30 s. In combat, when Fadia\u0027s HP drops below 20% , Baicang attacks the enemy 1 time, heals Fadia 1 time, and generates 1 Power Word Silence on target. Cooldown: 30 s. Switching to Baicang while Lacrimosa is in bat form can trigger 1 super jump for Baicang. Sure, we\u0027re all a bunch of eccentric weirdos who do our own thing, but we have our moments of perfect teamwork too. Spend enough time together, and your body starts to remember each other\u0027s habits and movements. What was that just now? Why, that was ETD-4\u0027s passionate combo, of course!","m":[]}],"how":"Baicang Firefly Hyper Baicang · Adler · Sakiri · Daffodill A high-damage Incantation-Scorch team centered around Baicang\u0027s Power Words and Dodge Charged Attacks, supported by buffs from Adler, Sakiri, and Daffodill\u0027s Phantom Step quick-swaps. Rotation Adler: Use his Ultimate and Redirect Skill first, as they do not benefit from Sakiri\u0027s ATK buff, and to grant the team a 10% Incantation Damage buff via Adler\u0027s R6. Sakiri: Use her Ultimate to apply her ATK buff to the team, then use her Redirect Skill (Devour Whole) to gain energy. Daffodill: Swap in and immediately use her Ultimate (Finale) to gain Phantom Step charges, then use her Redirect Skill (Resonance). Baicang: Swap in during Daffodill\u0027s skill animation. After Baicang\u0027s Ultimate (Judgment of Autumn), perform Basic Attacks 1 through 3 into his Redirect Skill (Generous Guidance). Daffodill: Swap in and use her first Phantom Step. Baicang: Swap back during Daffodill\u0027s Phantom Step animation. Baicang: Use his Dodge Charged Attack. Daffodill: Quickly swap in for her second Phantom Step. Baicang: Swap back before Phantom Step ends. Baicang: Spam his Dodge Charged Attack for the remainder of his Ultimate window, using Dodge Counters and his Redirect Skill (Generous Guidance) where applicable. Repeat from the first step with Adler, energy permitting. Tips \u0026 Tricks When Baicang applies a Power Word, it refreshes the duration of Scorch. Keep it up permanently by switching to Baicang and using one of his skills every 10 seconds or so. If a boss\u0027s HP is at 25% or lower and Baicang\u0027s Ultimate is about to come up, it may be beneficial to hold it to aim for the execute at 5% HP. Hold toward the enemy and Dodge to spam Baicang\u0027s Dodge Charged Attack. The animation of Baicang\u0027s Dodge Charged Attack can be cancelled after the words are thrown, allowing for very fast repeated use. When spamming his Dodge Charged Attack, you will sometimes get a Perfect Dodge. Perform a Dodge Counter in this situation to extend i-frames, since the Dodge Charged Attack has no i-frames.","pros":"Versatile, works well both against single-enemies, bosses and groups of mobs. Can execute low-HP targets instantly. Basic Attacks can help group enemies. Has self-sustain if played properly. Shop management buffs and can bonk customers. Looks silly with a sunflower head.","cons":"High skill ceiling, can be difficult to play and keep track of all his Power Words and stacks. Sacrifices self-HP when attacking, which may play against him unless the player manages to use Bless consistently. Execute only triggers during his Ult.","teams":[{"n":"Scorch Team","m":["daffodil","sakiri","adler, jiuyuan"],"c":"This team focuses on cycling all 3 of the Incantation units with Daffodill to stack and maintain Scorch. Biacang will be the one taking up the most field time on this team and deal a majority of the damage.","r":""},{"n":"Hexed Team","m":["nanally, mint","sakiri","jiuyuan"],"c":"The goal of this team is to cycle through everyone and keep up Hexed 100% of the time. Baicang and Nanally will be the dps in this dual-dps setup.","r":""}]},"Fadia":{"slug":"fadia","skills":[{"t":"Basic Attack","n":"Wordless Rejection","d":"Wordless Rejection Swings her cross shield and performs up to 5 consecutive attacks, dealing Psyche DMG . All Eyes on Me When Fadia\u0027s current HP is greater than 1 , she redirects a portion of damage taken by her teammates to herself before any shield mitigation is applied. Redirected damage cannot be further redistributed. Once Fadia\u0027s current HP drops to 1 , she ceases to redirect damage. At this point, if Fadia receives damage, she will share it with surviving teammates before any shield mitigation, and will absorb the remaining damage herself. Falling Contempt Swings her cross shield in the air and plunges, dealing 1 instance of Psyche DMG to an area upon impact. Increases DMG based on fall height, up to 100% . Critical Riposte: Evasion Trigger Triggers when casting Wordless Rejection after a Critical Dodge. Charges toward the target at high speed and deals 1 instance of Psyche DMG to an area, reducing Break. The most laughable thing about being alive is how you bow to self-evident meanings and submit to the power of orders. So why not laugh at you pitiful worms?","m":["1st Instance Ratio: 43.3%","2nd Instance Ratio: 29.7% + 36%","3rd Instance Ratio: 77.1%","4th Instance Ratio: 28.3% + 33.2%","5th Instance Ratio: 27.3% + 80.3%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Existence","d":"Come, have a taste of this. Deals 1 instance of Psyche DMG to an area and inflicts Destructive Experience on the enemy with the highest Max HP in the area for a period. During the duration, when Fadia takes damage, the target shares a percentage of the damage taken. Destructive Experience ends when the duration expires, when the Redirection DMG taken by the target reaches its cap, or when the target and Fadia leave combat. \"Oh hey—just a friendly tip from her teammate: attacking her right now might not be the smartest move…\"","m":["DMG Ratio: 1.6% + 2.5% + 2.5% Max HP","Destructive Experience Duration: 15s","Redirection DMG Ratio: 300%","Redirection DMG Cap: 8% Max HP","CD: 16s"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Agony to Euphoria","d":"Without pain, life closes in on itself. Enters Lilith state, dealing 6 instances of Mental DMG and restoring HP. Recasts Wordless Rejection while in Lilith state to perform up to 5 follow-up attacks, each dealing Mental DMG. Fully restores the energy of Agony to Euphoria when lost HP reaches the Destructive Threshold. Increases the damage and HP restored by Agony to Euphoria when it is cast with lost HP greater than or equal to the Destructive Threshold. Exits Lilith state when the duration ends, all 5 follow-up attacks are performed, characters are switched, or other skills of Fadia are used. \"Since the Director chose to exploit this instability, my duty is to observe and restrict it—to ensure such dangerous volatility stays within controllable bounds.\"","m":["1st Instance Ratio: 3.9% Max HP","2nd Instance Ratio: 1.2% ×4 Max HP","3rd Instance Ratio: 6.3% Max HP","1st Follow Up Ratio: 2% Max HP","2nd Follow Up Ratio: 3.2% + 3.6% Max HP"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Outsider","d":"Swings her cross shield, dealing 1 instance of Psyche DMG to an area. Move it, you\u0027re blocking the camera!","m":["DMG Ratio: 200%"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Furnace of Guilt","d":"Nova Enhancement : Allows all allies to drain Max HP from the target when Nova ends. The target loses Max HP equal to 200% of Fadia\u0027s base Max HP, and each ally gains Max HP equal to 10% of Fadia\u0027s base Max HP. Total drained cannot exceed 50% of Fadia\u0027s base Max HP. Restores both parties\u0027 stats upon exiting combat. More… MORE! Fill this void—if you can!","m":[]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Denial and Plunder","d":"Like a baby yearning for nourishment from mommy. When Fadia is in the team, increases team max HP by 10% . If you want it, go grab it.","m":[]}],"how":"$undefined","pros":"Strong damage mitigation through damage redirection, effectively acting as a pseudo shielder for the team. Good burst damage window in her Ultimate, with up to 5 follow-up attacks in enhanced state dealing Mental Damage which ignores common enemy resistance. She’s very hard to kill, as when she’s at 1 HP, she redirects damage to her teammates, and her Ultimate heals her. Provides passive off-field pressure by draining enemy HP when she is hit, allowing her to contribute consistent chip damage even when she is not actively on the field. Can get free gifts from male shop owners and gain extra satisfaction and tips from Swift Travel/Shop Management Buffs.","cons":"Damage redirection is limited in effectiveness against multiple enemies, making her more single-target focused by default. Unless you invest into her Awakening skill, Bringer of Love and Death , which allows her to target up to 10 enemies within range. Her kit wants her to lose health (aka the team being hit), which can be a bit antithetical to most teams. You want to manage your HP.","teams":[{"n":"Nova Team","m":["haniel","daffodil","aurelia"],"c":"This team focuses on causing the Nova reaction as often as possible to utilize Fadia’s HP drain, Haniel’s Attack drain, and Aurelia’s extra Nova damage.","r":""}]},"Zero":{"slug":"zero","skills":[{"t":"Basic Attack","n":"Appraisal","d":"Basic Attack: Appraisal - Severance Channels energy through the weapon, performing up to 5 consecutive attacks that deal Cosmos DMG . Basic Attack: Appraisal - Break Wields the weapon mid-air and plunges, dealing 1 instance of Cosmos DMG to an area upon impact. Increases DMG based on fall height, up to 100% . Critical Riposte: Flash of Inspiration Triggers when using Appraisal - Severance after a Critical Dodge. Seizes the opening from the enemy\u0027s missed attack and swings the weapon to counter, dealing 1 instance of Cosmos DMG to an area and reducing Break. Handling a sword is the only way I feel in control.","m":["1st Instance Ratio: 23%","2nd Instance Ratio: 22.4% + 25.9%","3rd Instance Ratio: 37.9% + 6.4% + 38.5%","4th Instance Ratio: 15.4% + 99.7%","5th Instance Ratio: 68.3%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Appraise and Engrave","d":"Opening, exposed! Performs 3 consecutive weapon strikes. Leaps into the air to charge. Fires an Esper Cannon that deals 1 instance of Cosmos DMG to an area. Deals an additional 1 instance of Cosmos DMG to the first enemy hit whose level is below Zero\u0027s own level. A surreal scene, outlined in slashes, emerges from thin air.","m":["Weapon Strike Ratio: 20% + 20% + 125.6% + 134.4%","Extra DMG Ratio: 200%","CD: 16s","Cycle Energy: 100"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Divide by Zero","d":"Sweeps away the unseen lines that connect the Nexus in a dance of blades. Deals multiple instances of Cosmos DMG to an area. I sense an Anomaly Nexus, bound by invisible, silent, intangible ties… All severed in an instant with a single graceful strike.","m":["DMG Ratio: 83.7% + 116.3%","CD: 15s","Costs Ultimate Energy: 100"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Rift Blossom","d":"Slashes through space and detonates a rift, dealing 2 instances of Cosmos DMG to an area.","m":["DMG Ratio: 83.7% + 116.3%"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Appraiser","d":"Charge Enhancement : Restores HP equal to 50% of Zero\u0027s Base ATK when the active character gains Ultimate Energy. Where will this ability to read and understand anomalies lead me?","m":[]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Anomaly Perception","d":"Ultimate: Divide by Zero damage increases by 25% . Zeroth Sense Synchronization","m":[]}],"how":"$undefined","pros":"Instantly enables Esper Cycles with Skill, making rotations much smoother Their Cosmos Attribute aligns well with their gameplay as it’s the most middle of the upper cycle enabling good rotation values for Blossom, Remora or Charge compositions. Low investment character and easy to use.","cons":"Doesn\u0027t have many additional effects or uniqueness to their kit aside from the Cycle Rate.","teams":[{"n":"Charge Team","m":["nanally, jiuyuan, mint","hathor, skia","haniel, sakiri"],"c":"This Charge team would focus on filling Hathor and Haniel’s Ultimates to upkeep buff uptime and deal strong burst damage.","r":""}]},"Chaos":{"slug":"chaos","skills":[{"t":"Basic Attack","n":"Pursuit","d":"Basic Attack: Pursuit Wields his weapon and performs up to 5 consecutive attacks, dealing Lakshana DMG . Basic Attack: Final Verdict Your guilt is plain to see. Hold Basic Attack to trigger Final Verdict. Consumes all Crimes to add a 2nd hit to Final Verdict and deal heavy Settlement DMG if current Crime is at its cap. Performs only the 1st hit of Final Verdict, dealing 1 instance of damage, if Crime has not reached its cap. Basic Attack: Overturn Press Basic Attack while airborne to plunge, dealing 1 instance of Lakshana DMG to an area upon impact. Increases DMG based on fall height, up to 1×. Intuition / Instinct Triggers when using Pursuit after performing a Critical Dodge. Swings his hatchet at the target, dealing 1 instance of Lakshana DMG and reducing Break. Honed over countless years.","m":["1st Instance DMG Ratio: 18.2%","2nd Instance DMG Ratio: 15.1% + 39%","3rd Instance DMG Ratio: 14.4%","4th Instance DMG Ratio: 26.8% + 10.2% ×2 + 86%","5th Instance DMG Ratio: 24.9% ×2 + 79.8%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Doubtmark","d":"Target traits confirmed. Fires at enemies ahead and summons his hound to pounce on the target. The hound bites the target back and forth twice. Inflicts Warrant on up to 2 enemies for 15s when the skill hits. Increases damage dealt by 20% when attacking targets with Warrant . Chaos can\u0027t remember when the hound first appeared. He only remembers missing the little dog from home, and then the hound was there.","m":["Bite DMG Ratio: 82.5% + 217.5%","Targets with Warrant: 2","Cycle Energy: 12","Builds up Crime: 100","Warrant Duration: 15s"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Retribution","d":"Summons his hound to suppress nearby enemies, inflicting Warrant on all enemies within range and entering the Dread Echo state. Increases Crime rapidly over time while Dread Echo is active, allowing Final Verdict to be cast more frequently to deal heavy Settlement DMG. Deep down, you know good and evil cycle endlessly, and none of it ever truly ends.","m":["Suppression DMG Ratio: 127.3% ×4 + 290.9%","Dread Echo Duration: 12s","Crime Generation Rate: 150/s","Warrant Duration: 15s","Costs Ultimate Energy: 100"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Onslaught","d":"Don\u0027t even think about running! Swings his scythe upward, dealing 1 instance of Lakshana DMG . United in purpose, through fair weather and foul, as they once were.","m":[]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Justice in Time","d":"Remora Enhancement : Deals Lakshana DMG equal to 800% of ATK to the target when Remora ends, based on Remora\u0027s duration. Each second beyond the base 5s duration increases total DMG by 45% , up to 300% . Resets Remora\u0027s duration when reapplied. Do you still believe every right answer leads to light?","m":[]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Prime Target","d":"Increases the damage bonus from Warrant to 30% . \"All forms filed. All approvals granted.\"","m":[]}],"how":"Chaos Remora Bomb Chaos · Zero (MC) · Hathor · Haniel This team enables both Remora and Stain, boosting Chaos\u0027s personal damage. The core gameplan is to apply Remora followed by Stain, then maximize damage output within the 20% damage and 10% Crit Rate buff window. Rotation Hathor: Start with Hathor and use her Redirect Skill just to put it on CD. Zero (MC): Switch to MC to trigger Remora and use their Ultimate. Haniel: Switch to Haniel and use her Redirect Skill (Silent Moonlit Forest Guardian) and Ultimate (A Melody Named Haniel) to apply the ATK and Crit Damage buff (at R6). Chaos: Swap to Chaos to trigger Stain. Chaos: Use his Redirect Skill to apply Warrant, followed by his Ultimate. While in the Dread Echo state, aim to do 2 enhanced Heavy Attacks. Hathor: Swap from Chaos to Hathor. Hathor: Use her Ultimate, followed by any available enhanced Skills. Repeat from the beginning, but using Chaos’s Gauge to trigger Stain and MC’s Skill to trigger Remora. Tips \u0026 Tricks Chaos does not need to be the one to trigger Remora for his enhancement passive to activate, but if he does not trigger it then make sure that Warrant is on the target before Remora explodes. Chaos’s additional “Crime” generation during his Ultimate is a large source of his Crime build up for his Enhanced Heavy attack. Aim to use it as frequently as possible, but be wary that the target won’t leave afterwards. Be careful not to refresh the Remora duration again before it explodes, you will simply be delaying the damage hit without increasing it any further. While under the effect of his Ultimate, you can start the Heavy Attack animation at 850+ crime and reach 1000 Crime during the initial animation to execute an enhanced Heavy Attack. However, his unenhanced Heavy attack does negligible damage and doesn’t generate any Crime, so be careful when doing this.","pros":"Strong burst window during Retribution, with Dread Echo rapidly ramping Crime generation while also applying Warrant to all enemies. Making his Ultimate Buff window deal very high damage. Remora Enhancement, especially when its duration is extended, helps deal significantly more DMG. Crime builds up simply by attacking, and Warrant can be inflicted through his Redirect Skill or Ultimate, making his kit function naturally since that is what you do, you hit things, you silly DPS. He can place custom teleport points on the map, has fishing buffs, and can take his mask on and off. The mask is definitely the most important.","cons":"Currently not a lot of good F2P Arc options. It is difficult for him to extend Remora Enhancement duration on his own, making him reliant on team support to maximize its damage. (Like Hathor)","teams":[{"n":"Remora Bomb Team","m":["zero","hathor","haniel, fadia"],"c":"This team can trigger both Remora and Stain to buff Chaos’s personal damage. The goal would be to trigger Remora and then Stain, then get as much damage under the 20% damage and 10% crit buff as possible.","r":""},{"n":"Chaos Charge Team","m":["zero, hotori","hathor","jiuyuan, mint, nanally"],"c":"The goal is to build up Cycle gauge on Chaos to trigger Remora with MC, and then instant cycle to Jiuyuan to trigger Blossom and Charge to fill up Chaos’s Ultimate. This team feels really smooth and has a bit higher Ultimate uptime than his Remora Bomb team, but will often perform slightly worse without his Awakenings.","r":""}]},"Daffodil":{"slug":"daffodil","skills":[{"t":"Basic Attack","n":"Still Waters","d":"Basic Attack: Still Waters Her heart is as calm as still waters, long accustomed to battle. Wields her twin blades to perform up to 5 consecutive attacks, dealing Chaos DMG . Basic Attack: Light Prism Light and shadow exist in separate realms. Daffodil\u0027s Break Damage contribution is increased by 20% . Basic Attack: Mirror on Water I am here. Hold Basic Attack to trigger. Dashes forward, performing a whirlwind slash and leaving behind marks, dealing Chaos DMG. Basic Attack: Displaced Edge Press dodge to trigger the special dodge action Displaced Edge during Still Waters. Grants invincibility during the action and does not interrupt the current combo. Basic Attack: Crosshair Lock Wields her weapon while airborne and plunges, dealing 1 instance of Chaos DMG to an area upon impact. Increases DMG based on fall height, up to 100% . Critical Riposte: Close Call Triggers when using Still Waters after performing a Critical Dodge. Instantly lifts her foot, pulling the rope to swing her blade toward the target, dealing 1 instance of Chaos DMG and reducing Break. Follow the muscle memory.","m":["1st Instance Ratio: 16.7%","2nd Instance Ratio: 15.3% + 15.3%","3rd Instance Ratio: 13.2% ×2 + 6.2% ×2 + 14.1% + 26.3%","4th Instance Ratio: 52.4% + 19.3% + 12.7%","5th Instance Ratio: 10.1% ×4 + 10.1% ×2 + 47.3%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Resonance","d":"Redirect Skill: Resonance Resonating with the blade. Deals damage to the target. Grants Resonance stacks and increases damage when any team member casts a Support Skill. Increases Resonance\u0027s DMG and Break per Support Skill cast, up to 2 stacks. Enhances Resonance and replaces it with Echoes when stacks reach the maximum. Redirect Skill: Echoes Resonance carries sound, echo responds in kind. Swiftly shifts her stance, swinging her blade with the rope to deal Chaos DMG to the target. A girl trapped in a beautiful garden was no more than a prisoner in a cave. But for a child with kaleidoscope eyes that could see through all things did she feel her way along the walls and stumble into a new world.","m":["Skill Ratio: 40.9% ×2 + 33.7% ×5 + 49.8%","Cycle Rate: 10","CD: 16s","Enhanced Skill Ratio: 34.8% ×6 + 91.1%","Cycle Energy: 10"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Finale","d":"Casts Finale, dealing Chaos DMG to enemies in an area. Unseals her left eye, increasing damage and inflicting Insight on nearby enemies for the duration. Unlocks the skill Phantom Step , which can be used up to 2 times. Casting Finale resets Phantom Step charges. \"I have lost everything. What exactly am I supposed to toast to?\" \"Do you need a reason to toast? Well… then let\u0027s toast to absolute despair, to skies we\u0027ve never seen, and to the one and only narcissus blooming in the heart of this lake.\"","m":["DMG Ratio: 49.3% ×3 + 25.3% ×3 + 51.1% ×7 + 218.3%","CD: 20s","Costs Ultimate Energy: 120","DMG Increase: 10%","Parry Attack Extra DMG Ratio: 300%"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Crossed Blades","d":"Leave the rest to me. Swings her blade in a slashing motion, dealing 1 instance of Chaos DMG to the target. The bodyguard at Eibon Antique Shop has always been reliable. Her clean, efficient skills inspire confidence that, as long as she\u0027s trusted, any problem can be solved with ease.","m":["DMG Ratio: 200%"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Blade Draw","d":"Discord Enhancement : Further reduces the target\u0027s Break cap by 10% for 30 s while affected by Discord and restores it to normal upon leaving combat. Stacks Discord Enhancement effects up to a maximum reduction of 30% of the target\u0027s initial Break cap. Beneath her expressionless façade, fleeting moments of tenderness may appear, like sunlight dancing on snow.","m":[]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Cicada Shell","d":"Increases Phantom Step DMG by 80% . She once wandered the gray borderlands like a machine, but now she has somewhere to call home.","m":[]}],"how":"$undefined","pros":"Strong fit for quickswap team structures, with minimal field time required Provides reliable Break-based control, effective even against bosses Converts team activity into damage through Support Skill synergy and Resonance scaling Can recharge her Ultimate, if parrying using Phantom Steps or support skill if Phantom Step is available. Can fit in a lot of teams. She can help with increasing traffic and reducing ingredient consumption rate for Shop Management and an Owner’s Selection ability to help with the minigame.","cons":"Requires high rotation discipline, since most of her damage scaling depends on frequent swapping. Does not perform as well in low switching teams. Break damage is contribution-based, so she loses a lot of value if the team is not built around Break.","teams":[{"n":"Discord Team","m":["sakiri","baicang, adler","haniel, fadia"],"c":"This team allows Daffodill to get her Discord proc and reduce the enemies’ max break bar; leading to easier breaks with each Discord reaction.","r":""},{"n":"Daffodil Scorch Team","m":["sakiri","baicang","adler"],"c":"This team focuses on cycling all 3 of the Incantation units with Daffodill to stack and maintain Scorch. Since Daffodill is the only Chaos character as of 1.0, she is required for this team to function.","r":""}]},"Mint":{"slug":"mint","skills":[{"t":"Basic Attack","n":"Perfect Containment","d":"Basic Attack: Perfect Containment Wields her weapon and performs up to 5 consecutive attacks, dealing Anima DMG . Basic Attack: Justice from Above Wields her weapon in the air and plunges, dealing 1 instance of Anima DMG to an area upon impact. Increases DMG based on fall height, up to 100% . Critical Riposte: Caramel Crisp Triggers when using Perfect Containment after a Critical Dodge. Leaps up to dodge an attack, seizes the enemy\u0027s opening, and swiftly swings her weapon, dealing 1 instance of Anima DMG to an area and reducing Break. Basic Attack: Minty Whirlwind Hold Basic Attack to make Mint dance and spin, forming a tornado that continuously drains Stamina and deals continuous Anima DMG to surrounding enemies. \"First place in the Containment Simulation Exam: Mint, from CSU-2.\"","m":["1st Instance Ratio: 10.4% + 23.1%","2nd Instance Ratio: 17%","3rd Instance Ratio: 26.2% + 34.1%","4th Instance Ratio: 18.4%","5th Instance Ratio: 25.5% + 52.3%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Ultimate: Super Claws","d":"Time to cool things down! Dashes forward, then returns to her original position, dealing 2 instances of AoE Anima DMG to enemies along the path. \"Ice cream is cool, mint is cool, so mint ice cream from Blizzi means double the happiness! Ooha — I\u0027m already shivering just thinking about it!\"","m":["DMG Ratio: 90% ×2","CD: 6s","Cycle Energy: 18"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Thunderous Whirlwind Slash","d":"Are you ready! Channels the surrounding wind into her dual blades, transforming them into wind blades that deal multiple instances of Anima DMG to an area. Lands with a final hit that deals massive Anima DMG to an area. The full name is \"Mint\u0027s Ultimate: Super Duper Ultra 360 Whirlwind Slash\", but I had to shorten it to what it is now because people wouldn\u0027t stop laughing about it.","m":["Impact DMG Ratio: 132.6%","Claw Combo Ratio: 58.8% ×5","Slash Ratio: 373.5%","CD: 15s","Costs Ultimate Energy: 100"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Ultimate: Invincible Tornado Slash","d":"Perfect finishing work from an elite member! Charges and leaps into the air, performing a penetrating attack on enemies, dealing 1 instance of Anima DMG to an area.","m":["DMG Ratio: 200%"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Transform! Super Mint!","d":"Blossom Enhancement : Expands Vita Pistils\u0027 damage area on hit. \"Watch closely now! I\u0027m not the same as before! You\u0027re now face-to-face with an elite operative!\"","m":[]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Bingo! We\u0027re Done Here!","d":"While Mint is on the field, her DEF is increased by 20% and her resistance to Interruptions is increased by 30% . There\u0027s always that extra burst of energy when work\u0027s almost done, especially when putting out new arrivals… \"Five minutes till close! Line up nicely and get nullified!\"","m":[]}],"how":"Mint Hyper Mint · Zero (MC) · Jiuyuan · Sakiri A Blossom-Hexed team built around Mint\u0027s Super Claws Redirect Skill spam and Charged Basic Attack (Minty Whirlwind), with Hexed reactions from Sakiri and Blossom from Jiuyuan and Zero. Rotation Zero (MC): Start on MC and use Ultimate and Redirect Skill, then switch to Mint. Mint: Use Mint\u0027s Redirect Skill (Super Claws), then switch to Sakiri. Sakiri: Use Sakiri\u0027s Ultimate and Redirect Skill (Devour Whole) to buff the team, then swap to Jiuyuan. Jiuyuan: Use Jiuyuan\u0027s Ultimate (Final Reckoning) and Redirect Skill, then swap back to Mint. Mint: Use Mint\u0027s Ultimate (Thunderous Whirlwind Slash) into Redirect Skill (Super Claws), then hold Basic Attack (Minty Whirlwind) until Hexed ends. Burst rotation complete. A Hexed proc remains for Mint into Sakiri. Repeat from the first step., keeping Hexed and Blossom procs in mind. Tips \u0026 Tricks Blossom always deals Anima Damage, so the Hexed status will also cause it to deal more damage. While holding a Charged Attack (Minty Whirlwind) on Mint, you can press Redirect Skill to cancel the animation and parry any incoming attacks. Mint\u0027s Charged Attack (Minty Whirlwind) will expire naturally after 5 seconds.","pros":"Free character, making her accessible to all players without any investment Very easy to learn and play, with a straightforward kit that does not require complex setups or timing Enjoyable and durable close-range playstyle that rewards staying on field as a main DPS, making her great for players who dislike quick-swapping. Can build up Cycle Rate slightly faster from just using her skills. Can ask for people’s cars without stealing them, shop management buffs. OHMYGAWDITSMINT","cons":"Her kit is very basic and not too much else is going on. She needs her A1 to actually function (Though you’ll get one of her copies for free, and you’ll get another copy of her soon enough).","teams":[{"n":"Blossom Team","m":["jiuyuan, nanally","haniel","zero, edgar"],"c":"This team focuses on dealing off-field damage in an AoE with Haniel and Blossom. Triggering the reaction as often as possible will increase DPS, and Mint serves as the main on-field DPS here. When switching into Edgar, you would do so for the reaction and then switch back off of him unless heals are needed.","r":""},{"n":"Mint Hypercarry Team","m":["sakiri","jiuyuan","zero, hotori"],"c":"This team will also perform strongly in AoE content due to having Blossom for extra damage, Hexed for another 20% damage, and both Sakiri and Jiuyuan for great crowd control . Additionally, Blossom damage is considered Anima damage so it gains a 20% boost from Hexed as well.","r":""}]},"Jiuyuan":{"slug":"jiuyuan","skills":[{"t":"Basic Attack","n":"When Secrets Take Shape","d":"Basic Attack: When Secrets Take Shape Dual-wields to perform up to 5 consecutive attacks, dealing Anima DMG . Grants 2 Rose Pact Bullets . Establishes a Lethal Rose Pact with the target when the final hit strikes. Basic Attack: Bird\u0027s Eye View Press Basic Attack while airborne to plunge, dealing 1 instance of Anima DMG to an area upon impact. Increases DMG based on fall height, up to 100% . Basic Attack: Info-Guided Arts Hold Basic Attack to trigger a branch attack that auto-targets and fires a bullet, dealing 1 instance of Anima DMG . Consumes Rose Pact Bullets for continuous fire and prioritizes targets with Lethal Rose Pact when Rose Pact Bullets are available. Basic Attack: Opportunity Lock-On Press Aim to enter Aim mode. Fires a bullet that deals 1 instance of Anima DMG to the enemy in the crosshair. Critical Riposte: Turning the Tide Triggers when using When Secrets Take Shape after a Critical Dodge. Swings both arms and fires in a cross pattern at targets in front, binding them with Lethal Rose Pact while dealing 1 instance of Anima DMG , reducing Break, and granting 2 Rose Pact Bullets . \"She glides through the city like a phantom, where light and shadow dance. Weaving secrets from whispers and fleeting leads, every move is a quiet vow to seal each deal in flawless harmony.\"","m":["1st Instance Ratio: 21.8%","2nd Instance Ratio: 24.1% + 9.3%","3rd Instance Ratio: 33.5% + 5.1% + 25.9%","4th Instance Ratio: 12.6% + 24.5% + 17.5% + 10.2%","5th Instance Ratio: 76%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Intel Hunter","d":"Dashes across the battlefield, pulling the target into the range of control and attacking. Deals multiple instances of Anima DMG and grants 4 Rose Pact Bullets while establishing a Lethal Rose Pact . We\u0027re pretty good at solving problems.","m":["DMG Ratio: 36% + 38.2% ×4 + 111.4%","Rose Pact Bullets Gained: 4","CD: 16s","Cycle Energy: 12"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Final Reckoning","d":"Dashes across the battlefield at high speed, continuously firing on surrounding targets before ending with a large-scale explosion, dealing Anima DMG . Triggers Final Reckoning, causing all Lethal Rose Pact targets within range to enter a stage where Pact Settlement can be triggered, executing all settlements simultaneously on the final hit. A faint stir in the air. Alas… merely a fleeting foe.","m":["DMG Ratio: 61.8% + 78.4% ×3 + 24.4% ×7 + 132.1%","CD: 15s","Costs Ultimate Energy: 100","Pact Settlement DMG Increased To: 400%","Pact Settlement grants Ultimate Energy: 40"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Intel Lock-On","d":"Fires a curved bullet, dealing 1 instance of Anima DMG and granting 2 Rose Pact Bullets upon hit. Don\u0027t worry, I\u0027ve always had an excellent memory.","m":["DMG Ratio: 200%"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Seize the Moment","d":"Blossom Enhancement : Spawns 1 additional Vita Bud and increases Vita Bud limit on field to 6 . Went as smoothly as I thought it would.","m":[]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Whispers at My Command ","d":"Binds targets not affected by Lethal Rose Pact when Vita Pistils hit them. Triggers an additional settlement on targets already bound, causing them to take an extra 15% x Anima DMG . People say opportunities are rare, but I\u0027ve always been good at seizing them.","m":[]}],"how":"$undefined","pros":"Improves the Blossom Esper Cycle. Flexible, good against groups of enemies and single-target alike. Can gather enemies with her skill. Works both as on-field and off-field DPS.","cons":"Only efficient in Blossom teams. Utility locked behind Awakenings.","teams":[{"n":"Blossom Team","m":["zero","nanally, mint","edgar"],"c":"Jiuyuan just existing in a team that triggers Blossom doubles the damage output by creating two Vita Buds at a time. The goal with this team is to have two characters of each Attribute to maximize Vita Bud uptime on the field.","r":""},{"n":"Jiuyuan Charge Team","m":["zero","nanally, mint","hathor"],"c":"Due to Blossom lasting 10 seconds and Remora only lasting 5 seconds, you always want to trigger Blossom first when aiming for Charge. With Jiuyuan’s Vita Buds it is possible to get 2 separate energy ticks from one set of Buds, but this is basically random and based on the enemies’ positioning.","r":""}]},"Akane Rin":{"slug":"akane-rin","skills":[{"t":"Basic Attack","n":"Stringblade","d":"Basic Attack: Stringblade Performs up to 4 consecutive attacks using an electric guitar and Feathered Sound Blade, dealing Lakshana DMG . Generates String Energy whenever Akane Rin deals DMG to a target. String Energy has a cap of 30 . Basic Attack: Stage Dive Press Basic Attack while airborne to plunge, dealing 1 instance of Lakshana DMG in an area upon impact. Increases DMG based on fall height, by up to 100% . Critical Riposte: Featherblade Reverb Triggers when pressing Basic Attack after a Critical Dodge. Blasts the target with Feathered Sound Blade, dealing Lakshana DMG . Preserves Stringblade\u0027s combo stage when Stringblade is used within a certain time after casting Featherblade Reverb. Even the simplest strum can carry the power to stir the soul.","m":["Stringblade 1st Instance: Base DMG Ratio \u0026 String Energy Gained: 14% ×2, 1","Stringblade 2nd Instance: Base DMG Ratio \u0026 String Energy Gained: 21% ×2, 1","Stringblade 3rd Instance: Base DMG Ratio \u0026 String Energy Gained: 10% ×3 + 13% ×4, 2","Stringblade 4th Instance: Base DMG Ratio \u0026 String Energy Gained: 424%, 6","Stringblade Cycle Energy: 24"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Rhythm Wave","d":"Redirect Skill: Rhythm Wave Offers two casting methods for Akane Rin\u0027s Rhythm Wave. Press: Inflicts Overtone on the target for 25s and deals Lakshana DMG . Causes Overtone to resonate when Akane Rin launches a Basic Attack, relaying this attack over long range to the affected target and increasing the DMG Ratio of the relayed Stringblade or Featherblade Reverb by a certain amount. Hold: Deploys a Reverb Field for 25s and deals Lakshana DMG to enemies within range. Causes Reverb Field to resonate when Akane Rin performs a Basic Attack, relaying this attack through the field to deal 1 instance of Basic Attack DMG to all enemies within range and increasing the DMG of the relayed Stringblade or Featherblade Reverb by an additional amount. Allows only one Overtone or Reverb Field to exist at a time. Replaces the existing form when a new form is successfully established. Shares the same cooldown between both casting methods and allows either form to be selected again once the cooldown ends. Press Redirect Skill to cast Synced Resonance when String Energy reaches 30 and an active Overtone or Reverb Field is present. Triggers different enhanced effects based on the current form: Overtone : deals 1 instance of massive single-target Lakshana DMG to the affected target. Reverb Field : deals 1 instance of massive Lakshana DMG to enemies within range. Consumes 30 String Energy when Synced Resonance hits and consumes none if it misses. Preserves the existing Overtone or Reverb Field without refreshing its remaining duration. Grants Akane Rin invincibility and immunity to hitstun while casting Synced Resonance. Synced Resonance has no independent cooldown and does not affect Rhythm Wave\u0027s normal cooldown. Prevents Synced Resonance from being cast when neither Overtone nor Reverb Field is active, requiring pressing or holding Rhythm Wave to establish a form first. Amid applause and cheers, let the music swell like a tide and reach everyone in its path.","m":["Overtone DMG Ratio \u0026 String Energy Gained: 360%, 6","Cycle Energy from Overtone: 6","Reverb Field DMG Ratio \u0026 String Energy Gained: 162% ×2, 6","Cycle Energy from Reverb Field: 8","Overtone: Synced Resonance DMG Ratio: 1125%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Sonic Boom","d":"Casts the first instance of Sonic Boom, dealing multiple instances of massive Lakshana DMG to enemies within the target area and entering Solo Cadenza for 20s . Increases her Resistance to Interruptions while the state is active. Allows the second instance to be cast by pressing Sonic Boom again at any time after Solo Cadenza has been active for 4s , ending Solo Cadenza early, dealing 1 instance of massive Lakshana DMG to enemies within the target area. Requires the second instance to be cast manually. Does not automatically cast the second instance when Solo Cadenza ends. The second instance becomes unavailable if not cast before Solo Cadenza ends. Solo Cadenza functions independently of Overtone and Reverb Field and does not remove or replace either effect. Grants Akane Rin 3 Ultimate Energy per second while she is out of combat. \"Now that\u0027s what I call music!\" a fan in the crowd exclaimed, tears streaming down their face.","m":["1st Instance DMG Ratio: 64% ×10","2nd Instance DMG Ratio: 918%","Ultimate Cooldown: 20s","Ultimate Energy Cost: 100"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Altered Chord","d":"Strikes the strings with a powerful strum, dealing 1 instance of Lakshana DMG . A truly great guitarist always knows exactly when to kick in.","m":["DMG Ratio \u0026 String Energy Gained: 200%, 4"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Perfect Pitch","d":"Remora Enhancement : Grants Akane Rin an enhancement that lasts until she leaves combat after the team triggers Remora for the first time. Applies Remora to the target affected by Overtone and to all enemies within Reverb Field every 3s . Deals Lakshana DMG (counts as Redirect Skill DMG) equal to 150% of Akane Rin\u0027s ATK whenever the team reapplies Remora to an affected target. Increases this DMG by 20% for each 1s of Remora duration remaining on the target, up to 160% . Calculates each target\u0027s remaining Remora duration independently. Triggers this DMG no more than once per target every 1s . With perfect pitch, Akane Rin can tune any instrument by ear—no tools required. She\u0027s basically a tuner in human form.","m":[]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Starlit Anthem","d":"Increases Akane Rin\u0027s ATK by 20% for 20s after casting Sonic Boom. This effect does not stack. Resets the duration when triggered again. The starlight shimmering across the stage is proof of who she truly is.","m":[]}],"how":"Akane-Blackbird-Zero-Linko An Akane main DPS team that utilises Blackbird and Zero\u0027s instant cycles to frequently trigger Remora, Stain, Blossom and Charge. Blackbird will act as the sub DPS and damager dealer during Akane\u0027s downtime. Linko provides valuable RES reduction for the whole team and her Redirect Skill and Ultimate can summon Akane to further generate String Energy, which helps condense Akane\u0027s rotation. Zero: Use Ultimate and Redirect Skill, then swap to Akane to trigger Remora. Akane: Use Redirect skill (click the skill button against single target bosses that move around frequently, hold the button against stationary targets or groups of enemies), then swap to Linko. Linko: Use Redirect Skill and pick Akane, then swap to Blackbird. Blackbird: Use Redirect Skill, then swap to Akane to trigger Stain. Akane: Swap to Blackbird. Blackbird: Use the 1st Ultimate, then continue to Basic Attack until the enhanced Redirect Skill is ready. Use the enhanced Redirect Skill followed by the 2nd Ultimate, then swap to Linko. Linko: Use Ultimate, then swap to Akane. Akane: Use the 1st Ultimate, then continue to Basic Attack until the enhanced Redirect Skill is ready. Use the enhanced redirect skill followed by the 2nd Ultimate, then swap to Linko. Linko: Use Redirect Skill and pick Akane, then swap to Akane. Akane: Basic Attack until the enhanced Redirect Skill is ready. Use the enhanced redirect skill and swap to Zero to trigger Remora. Zero: Use Ultimate and Redirect skill, then swap to Linko to trigger Blossom. Linko: Swap to Akane. Akane: Use Redirect skill, then swap to Linko. From here, begin to repeat the rotation from when Akane first swapped to Linko. Tips and Tricks You can hold the Basic Attack Button to make Akane loop her Basic Attack chain. Akane does not have a Charged Attack. Try to let Akane finish her 4th and final Basic Attack in the attack chain as it deals the most damage and generates the most String Energy. Always pick Akane during Linko\u0027s Redirect Skill to generate more String Energy for Akane.","pros":"Can keep Remora uptime at essentially 100% as long as you land her Redirect Skill. Works well against both bosses and groups, with Overtone for single targets and Reverb Field for AoE. Fits well into Charge teams as either a Main DPS or quickswap, and benefits from Stain to boost her Lakshana DMG. Good DMG as expected of someone who’s labeled a Main DPS. She can play the guitar so you can probably play about 6-7 songs. Wow, cafe boosts. Wow, super sound buff. (Do people play this for the weeklies?)","cons":"Overtone can be a bit harder to land against fast enemies, but it\u0027s not a real issue since you can always hold Redirect Skill instead. You need to manually activate the second stage of her Ultimate before Solo Cadenza ends, or you lose the extra DMG.","teams":[{"n":"Stain Dual DPS","m":["blackbird","zero","linko"],"c":"The goal of this team is to always use support skills into Akane to boost her String Energy and use as many enhanced skills as possible.","r":""},{"n":"Shinku Revival","m":["akane-rin","iroi","zero"],"c":"Akane enables permanent Remora for Shinku\u0027s team, allowing her rotations to be smoother and provides a sorely lacking SubDPS option for the team.","r":""},{"n":"Akane Hyper","m":["blackbird","sakiri","iroi, haniel"],"c":"This team utilizes as many characters as possible to buff Akane during her main damage window. You are aiming to land 2 enhanced skills and both ults in the buff windows.","r":""}]},"Zankou":{"slug":"zankou","skills":[{"t":"Basic Attack","n":"Wildfire","d":"Basic Attack: Wildfire Wields her blade and performs up to 5 consecutive attacks while in Reality Form, dealing Incantation DMG . Pulls in targets within range on the 5th instance of Basic Attack. Gains the Hunt buff for the attack\u0027s duration. Basic Attack: Nightmare Waltz Wields her blade to pull the silk and performs up to 4 consecutive attacks while in Illusion Form, dealing Incantation DMG and inflicting 1 stack of Heartwrench on hit. Pulls in targets within range on the 3rd instance of Basic Attack. Each Nightmare Waltz attack spreads up to 4 DoT effects from the target to all enemies in the area, including the original target. Gains the Delusion buff for the attack\u0027s duration. The DMG dealt by Nightmare Waltz counts as Follow-up Attack DMG. Basic Attack: Flickering Shadow Hold Basic Attack during the 1st or 2nd stage of Wildfire while in Reality Form to trigger Flickering Shadow, dealing Incantation DMG . Basic Attack: Moonfall Hold Basic Attack during the 1st or 2nd stage of Nightmare Waltz while in Illusion Form to trigger Moonfall, dealing Incantation DMG . Inflicts 1 stack of Heartwrench on hit. The DMG dealt by Moonfall counts as Follow-up Attack DMG. Basic Attack: Broken Twigs Press Basic Attack while airborne to plunge, dealing 1 instance of Incantation DMG in an area upon impact. Increases DMG based on fall height by up to 100% . Critical Riposte: Voidstep Press Basic Attack after a Critical Dodge to deal Incantation DMG and reduce Break. The nightmare drifts in, and despair burns from within.","m":["Wildfire 1st Instance DMG Ratio: 15.8% + 27.4%","Wildfire 2nd Instance DMG Ratio: 35.2%","Wildfire 3rd Instance DMG Ratio: 57.8% + 18.3% + 35.3%","Wildfire 4th Instance DMG Ratio: 68.2% + 24.7% + 22.8% + 52.2% + 10.3%","Wildfire 5th Instance DMG Ratio: 36.4% ×2 + 12.6% ×2 + 96.5% + 63.4%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Sanguine Dash ","d":"Redirect Skill: Sanguine Dash Switches to Illusion Form after successfully casting Sanguine Dash while in Reality Form. Enables an enhanced Sanguine Dash for a set time after the 4th or 5th stage of Wildfire, Flickering Shadow, or Voidstep. Inflicts Heartwrench on targets hit and triggers Disarray, reducing massive Break of enemies in a large area. Delays the removal of the Reality Form Hunt effect when switching to Illusion Form with Sanguine Dash. Prevents the form switch if the skill is interrupted before it is complete. Redirect Skill: Soulcross Switches to Reality Form after successfully casting Soulcross while in Illusion Form. Enables an enhanced Soulcross shortly before Illusion Form ends. Deals massive DMG to enemies in a large area, inflicts Heartwrench on targets hit, and triggers Oblivion, activating Bloodfeast Reverie. Grants Illusion Form for a set duration. Ends Illusion Form and returns Zankou to Reality Form when Soulcross or Bloodfeast Reverie is successfully cast, when its duration expires, or when Zankou leaves the field. Delays the removal of the Illusion Form Delusion effect when switching to Reality Form with Soulcross. Counts all DMG dealt by Soulcross and its enhanced version as Follow-up Attack DMG. Prevents the form switch if the skill is interrupted before it is complete. No need to wake up yet. The nightmare is only beginning.","m":["Sanguine Dash DMG Ratio: 22.5% ×4 + 60%","Enhanced Sanguine Dash DMG Ratio: 26.3% ×4 + 70%","Soulcross DMG Ratio: 13.2% ×2 + 26.8% ×4 + 166.5%","Enhanced Soulcross DMG Ratio: 19.8% ×2 + 40.1% ×4 + 249.8%","Illusion Form Duration: 8s"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Inferno Flamenco","d":"Press to cast the Ultimate when Ultimate Energy is full. Has 2 Ultimates: Inferno Flamenco and Bloodfeast Reverie. Casts Inferno Flamenco if Bloodfeast Reverie is inactive. Prioritizes Bloodfeast Reverie if it is active. Counts DMG dealt by Bloodfeast Reverie as Follow-up Attack DMG and inflicts Vile Ash on enemies in a large area. Enables one enhanced Inferno Flamenco to be cast without consuming Ultimate Energy within a limited time after successfully casting Bloodfeast Reverie. Removes this cast opportunity when the time limit expires. The soul\u0027s flame dies within the dream, slipping into a sleep with no need to wake.","m":["Inferno Flamenco DMG Ratio: 125.1% + 294.9%","Enhanced Inferno Flamenco DMG Ratio: 163.8% + 386.2%","Bloodfeast Reverie DMG Ratio: 60.3% ×3 + 519%","Costs Ultimate Energy: 120","Enhanced Inferno Flamenco Follow-up Attack Window: 5s"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Stoked Flame","d":"Wields her blade to attack, dealing 1 instance of Incantation DMG . Fear is the finest fuel.","m":["Stoked Flame DMG Ratio: 200%"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Silent Sunset","d":"Scorch Enhancement : Scorch can be stacked up to 3 times. For each DoT effect allies inflict on a target afflicted with Scorch, Zankou inflicts 1 stack of Scorch on them, replacing the DMG, type, and duration of existing Scorch on the target with those of the newly inflicted effect. Scorch inflicted by this effect cannot trigger it again. Countless flames merge into a silent sun, burning every gaze into the same hue.","m":[]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Crimson Reverie","d":"Sets Zankou\u0027s Cycle Energy to 100 upon entering battle. Cooldown: 30s . Triggers only once per battle. Increases Zankou\u0027s Cycle Intensity by 100 while she is on the team. Lose yourself in the intoxicating crimson of her gaze, and never wake again.","m":[]}],"how":"Zankou · Iroi · Sakiri · Daffodill A high-damage Incantation-Scorch team focused on Zankou’s Ultimate and Damage Over Time effects, supported by buffs from Iroi and Sakiri, and Daffodill\u0027s Phantom Step quick-swaps. Rotation Zankou: Swap to Daffodill to trigger Scorch. Daffodill: Use Ultimate and then Redirect Skill, then swap to Sakiri. Sakiri: Use her Ultimate to apply her ATK buff to the team, then use her Redirect Skill (Devour Whole) to gain energy. Iroi: Swap in and trigger Hexed in the process. Use her Ultimate, followed by her Skill to apply the attack buff to the team. During the skill animation, swap into Daffodill. Daffodill: Use a Phantom Step and then swap to Zankou. Zankou: Use Heavy Attack, followed by Enhanced Skill. Then, basic attack or heavy attack for 5 seconds to build DoT stacks until her second Enhanced Skill (Soulcross) is available. Zankou: After using her second Enhanced Skill, she should have her Enhanced Ultimate. Right after this, we are going to use her Ultimate Finisher and then heavy attack into enhanced skill again. Auto attack until we are at 10 stacks of the second DoT and then switch off her. Daffodill: Swap in and use her second Phantom Step and the Youthful Fantasy Arc to prepare for a break. Iroi: Swap back during Daffodill\u0027s Phantom Step animation to reapply the attack buff with her Skill. Zankou: Switching to Zankou here should trigger Hexed again, and you will be aiming to get to her Enhanced Soulcross again. After this, the goal will be to build energy on any characters that don’t have their Ultimate yet and then restart the rotation from the top. Tips \u0026 Tricks You can gain access to Zankou’s Enhanced Skill 1 by doing Basic 1 through 5, dodge countering, or heavy attacking. If you do another action before you press the skill, it will revert to its regular form. Due to her Passive 1, Zankou can start any fight by swapping into a Chaos unit to put on Scorch. She can easily stack this Scorch to 3 and keep it up permanently with her own DoTs. Since swapping off of the field while Zankou is in Illusion will result in the buff falling off, the main times that you can swap with her without interrupting her rotation are after her Soulcross skill and after her Bloodfeast Reverie Ultimate (for 5 seconds before the timer for Inferno Flamenco expires).","pros":"Instant Cycle burst, as she gains 100 Cycle Energy at the start of every battle, allowing her to form an Esper Cycle right away. She also gains +100 Cycle Intensity. She constantly applies and spreads DoT, making her strong in Scorch teams. Every attack in Illusion counts as Follow-Up Damage, giving her synergy with teams that rely on it, such as Hexed teams. Her gameplay looks complicated on paper, but it’s really just about using her Redirect Skill and not very much else. Can turn invisible outside combat, becoming undetectable and gaining 50% movement speed for 20 seconds. Works in Pink Paw Heist too.","cons":"Being interrupted while using Redirect can disrupt her rotation and prevent her from properly triggering the effects tied to switching states. It can take a while to get through her rotation to apply her second DoT effect.","teams":[{"n":"Zankou Hyper","m":["sakiri","iroi, haniel","daffodil"],"c":"Zankou’s main DPS team that capitalizes on all of the aspects of her kit. She will on field for most of the time, while Iroi’s goal is to get Hexed and apply attack buffs. The same is true for Sakiri, and Daffodill is used to quickswap with Zankou and apply Ultimate before breaking.","r":""},{"n":"Zankomosa DoT","m":["sakiri","lacrimosa","haniel"],"c":"This team utilizes Zankou as a SubDPS for Lacrimosa to upkeep all of her DoTs and maximize Sakiri\u0027s buffs. Since Scorch is permanent in this team, any time Lacrimosa gets full cycle gauge she will switch to Haniel to proc DIscord/Nova for extra damage.","r":""},{"n":"Scarlet Break","m":["baicang, sakiri","adler","daffodil"],"c":"The goal of this team is to deal as much damage as possible per break. Sakiri/Baicang and Adler are meant to be built with Break Intensity, and Adler using “The Great Thief” Arc. This team does exceedingly well with Daffodill and Zankou both A1, using their respective Awakening 5s. You can just Ultimate on Daffodill, and then enhanced Skill on Zankou and everything dies!","r":""}]},"Haniel":{"slug":"haniel","skills":[{"t":"Basic Attack","n":"Paranormal Entrance","d":"Basic Attack: Paranormal Entrance Fires magic projectiles and performs up to 5 consecutive attacks, dealing Psyche DMG . Basic Attack: Paranormal Cannon Hold Basic Attack during the 1 st hit to charge, then fire a charged cannon forward. Basic Attack: Paranormal Entrance Press Basic Attack while airborne to plunge, dealing 1 instance of Psyche DMG to an area upon impact. Increases DMG based on fall height, up to 100% . Critical Riposte: Ace Sweep Triggers when casting Genesse Technique after a Critical Dodge. \"Being this slow will get us customer complaints, you know?\" Dodges the attack, dealing 1 instance of Psyche DMG , and reducing Break. Immediately releases fully charged Paranormal Cannon once. The difference between magic tricks and real magic? As long as you believe, it exists… Like conjuring orbs with your bare hands?","m":["1st Instance Ratio: 41.9%","2nd Instance Ratio: 11.2% ×2","3rd Instance Ratio: 58.2%","4th Instance Ratio: 15.6% ×4","5th Instance Ratio: 52.8%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Silent Moonlit Forest Guardian","d":"\"O owl of the quiet, moonlit forest depths, answer my call!\"* Throws her portable speaker Hootie, dealing Psyche DMG to an area. Grants the Team an ATK bonus based on Haniel\u0027s Base ATK while Hootie is active. Grants Hootie 1 stack of Four-Part Harmony when the current character attacks, up to 1 stack every 0.5 s. Accumulating 4 stacks of Four-Part Harmony triggers Ensemble , dealing Psyche DMG to enemies in an area around Hootie. Only 1 Hootie can exist at a time. Casting again refreshes Hootie\u0027s duration. Hootie remains when switching characters. O owl of the quiet, moonlit forest depths, I, Haniel, hereby forge a contract with you! … Come on, Hootie, work with me here.","m":["DMG Ratio: 100% ×2","Spread DMG Ratio: 20%","ATK Bonus Ratio: 10%","Duration: 8s","CD: 20s"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"A Melody Named Haniel","d":"Genesse Girls\u0027 Academy Paranormal Department! Assuming control! Releases an enhancement field centered on herself and gaining the Paranormal Ace effect for a period of time. Grants the Team an ATK bonus based on Haniel\u0027s Base ATK. Triggering Ensemble simultaneously triggers 1 additional Ensemble — Symphony effect around the character with increased DMG and range. Ensemble — Symphony does not grant Plot Armor for Haniel. When triggering Ensemble , the current active character\u0027s next attack deals additional damage for 3 s. Effect does not stack. While Paranormal Ace is active, Hootie\u0027s duration timer is paused until the end of the effect. You won\u0027t find Genesse Girls\u0027 Academy on any map of Hethereau, and naturally you won\u0027t find the Paranormal Department either. This story begins with Haniel\u0027s first serialized novel…","m":["DMG Ratio: 300%","Spread DMG Ratio: 30%","Enhanced Attack DMG Ratio: 30%","ATK Bonus Ratio: 10%","Duration: 10s"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Easter Egg Time","d":"Don\u0027t be so boring! How about a little easter egg? Fires 1 magic projectile at the enemy, dealing 1 instance of Psyche DMG .","m":["DMG Ratio: 200%"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"It\u0027s Friendship!","d":"Nova Enhancement : Allows all allies to drain ATK from the target when Nova ends. The target loses ATK equal to 4% of Haniel\u0027s Base ATK, and each ally gains ATK equal to 8% of Haniel\u0027s Base ATK. The total drain is capped at 16% of Haniel\u0027s Base ATK, and the target cannot lose more than 20% of their initial ATK. Restores both parties\u0027 stats upon exiting combat. For Haniel, she\u0027d rather hear lively stories about companions than lonely tales of heroism. Even a bunch of hot-headed fools would be fine.","m":[]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"It\u0027s Bond!","d":"Grants Haniel 1 stack of Plot Armor when the current character triggers Ensemble , increasing the ricochet cap of Paranormal Cannon. Grants 1 stack of Plot Armor per Ensemble trigger. Grants 2 stacks of Plot Armor per Ensemble trigger while Haniel is in Paranormal Ace state. Can accumulate up to 4 stacks of Plot Armor . Sports anime makes you want to play sports. Band anime makes you want to learn an instrument. Battle anime — well, I wouldn\u0027t recommend trying it.","m":[]}],"how":"$undefined","pros":"Provides strong, consistent team-wide ATK buffs that remain active even when she is off-field. Very easy to fit into most team compositions due to her universal support utility. With Awakenings, her buff uptime is very good. Offers additional offensive value through periodic AoE-triggered effects via Ensemble. Helps with Shop Management.","cons":"Loses access to her passive without Chaos Attribute teammates.","teams":[{"n":"Nova Team","m":["daffodil","fadia","hathor, skia"],"c":"This team can trigger both Nova and Stain to buff Haniel or Hathor’s personal damage. The goal would be to trigger Stain and get as much damage under the 20% buff as possible. Hathor also extends Remora and buffs Crit rate with it, allowing the team to deal even more damage in this window.","r":""}]},"Adler":{"slug":"adler","skills":[{"t":"Basic Attack","n":"Deliverance","d":"Basic Attack: Deliverance Wields his weapon and performs up to 5 consecutive attacks, dealing Incantation DMG . Basic Attack: Liberation Enters aim mode, dealing 1 instance of single-target Incantation DMG to the enemy in the crosshair. Basic Attack: Ignorance Plunges, dealing 1 instance of Incantation DMG to an area upon impact. Increases DMG based on fall height, up to 100% . Critical Riposte: Revelation Triggers when casting Deliverance after a Critical Dodge. Dodges an attack with a quick dash, seizes the enemy\u0027s opening and swiftly swings his weapon, dealing 1 instance of Incantation DMG to an area, reducing their Break. Karma Grants Adler 1 stack of Karma when Deliverance or Ignorance hits an enemy. Grants Adler 2 stacks of Karma when Liberation hits an enemy. Max Karma stacks: 20 . A cane makes for quite the fitting accessory… a gentleman\u0027s weapon.","m":["1st Instance Ratio: 20.1%","2nd Instance Ratio: 57.7%","3rd Instance Ratio: 15.4% x2","4th Instance Ratio: 21.9% + 23.1% + 74.6%","5th Instance Ratio: 87.5%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Evil\u0027s Bane","d":"Need help? Summons Sunya phantoms to strike enemies, dealing 1 instance of Incantation DMG to an area, then inflicting Incantation DMG over time on enemies and granting active characters a shield with Blessing. Consumes all stacks of Karma on skill cast. Each stack consumed grants Adler 2% Skill DMG. \"This commission… let\u0027s get to know our target first. We…\" \"Coluccis! Roll out!\" \"…Stay safe, I\u0027ll handle everything else.\"","m":["1st Instance Ratio: 70% DEF ×3","DoT Ratio: 20% DEF","Shield Ratio: 1,000 + 80% DEF","DoT Duration: 10s","DoT Interval: 1s"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Tranquility","d":"I wish not fight if possible. Summons Rupa, Vedana, Sanna, Vinnana, and Sankhara, 5 Sunyas in total, to strike all enemy targets. Each target takes 5 instances of Incantation DMG . When only a single enemy remains on the field, Sunyas will perform a second strike, dealing a total of 10 instances of Incantation DMG . The folks at Eibon like to guess the names of Adler\u0027s Sunyas. When they guess correctly, Adler rewards them with handmade desserts!","m":["Single DMG Ratio: 100% DEF","CD: 20s","Costs Ultimate Energy: 120"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Pristine Reflection","d":"This fight shall not be prolonged any longer. Aims and fires 1 Compressed Round at the enemy, dealing 1 instance of Incantation DMG to an area on hit.","m":["DMG Ratio: 200%"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Temperance","d":"Scorch Enhancement: Applies one of three random debuffs whenever Scorch is inflicted on a target: -20% ATK, -10% Esper RES, or +10% Break Efficiency, lasting for 15 s. The same effect cannot stack. A meticulously pressed uniform and even hair, even in battle. The butler\u0027s first lesson is to maintain an impeccable appearance.","m":[]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Righteous Heart","d":"Adler DEF +20% \"Sometimes a forceful strategy is preferable to lengthy negotiations.\"","m":[]}],"how":"$undefined","pros":"Offers a wide range of utility in the form of debuffs and a shield. Needs little field-time to do his job.","cons":"Low damage and overall stats due to scaling off of DEF. Also because of that, he doesn’t synergize well with most buffers.","teams":[{"n":"Scorch Team","m":["daffodil","baicang","sakiri"],"c":"Adler’s main role in this team is to wield “The Great Thief” Arc to buff everyone’s Break Intensity which increases the damage dealt by each break. He should also cast his shield as often as possible because it will also apply a DoT and increase Incantation DMG (at A6).","r":""},{"n":"Hexed Team","m":["nanally, mint","sakiri","jiuyuan"],"c":"Adler provides shielding in this team and wants to use his Skill and Ultimate under Hexed to maximize their damage. With 2 characters of each attribute it is possible to maintain Hexed 100% of the time.","r":""}]},"Blackbird":{"slug":"blackbird","skills":[{"t":"Basic Attack","n":"Fleeting Shadow","d":"Basic Attack: Fleeting Shadow Uses Chain Cage to perform up to 5 consecutive attacks, dealing Psyche DMG . Gains Malice after hitting an enemy. Basic Attack: Roostcall Hold Basic Attack during the 1st, 2nd, or 3rd hit of Fleeting Shadow to trigger Roostcall, imprisoning the target with Chain Cage, dealing Psyche DMG , and greatly reducing their Movement Speed for a set duration. Gains Malice after hitting an enemy. Basic Attack: Lingering Affliction Press Basic Attack while airborne to plunge, dealing 1 instance of Psyche DMG to an area upon impact. Increases DMG based on fall height by up to 100% . Gains Malice after hitting an enemy. Critical Riposte: Avian Instinct Triggers when Blackbird uses Fleeting Shadow after a Critical Dodge, attacking the target to deal Psyche DMG . Gains Malice after hitting an enemy. Basic Attack: Pyreflame Blackbird is engulfed in flames, and the Witch of Deliverance emerges from the blaze, unleashing up to 5 consecutive attacks that deal Psyche DMG . Consumes Malice after hitting an enemy. Basic Attack: Bestowed Grace Hold Basic Attack during the 2nd hit of Pyreflame to trigger Bestowed Grace. The Witch of Deliverance rises into the air, briefly charges up, then deals Psyche DMG over a large area. Consumes Malice after hitting an enemy. Basic Attack: Tidings Unto All Hold Basic Attack during Bestowed Grace or Flames of Deliverance to trigger Tidings Unto All, dealing multiple instances of Psyche DMG to the target. Consumes Malice after hitting an enemy. Basic Attack: Searing Scar Press Basic Attack while the Witch of Deliverance is airborne to plunge, dealing 1 instance of Psyche DMG to an area upon impact. Increases DMG based on fall height, by up to 100% . Consumes Malice after hitting an enemy. Critical Riposte: Born of Calamity Triggers when the Witch of Deliverance uses Pyreflame after a Critical Dodge, attacking the target to deal Psyche DMG . Consumes Malice after hitting an enemy. Invocation Generates varying amounts of Malice upon casting Fleeting Shadow, Roostcall, Lingering Affliction, Avian Instinct, Last Word, or Netherplume Rite. Grants Malice immediately upon entering battle. Prevents Malice from being gained while in the Witch of Deliverance state. Allows Malice to be consumed after casting Pyreflame, Searing Scar, Bestowed Grace, Tidings Unto All, Born of Calamity, Flames of Deliverance, or Naught but Mercy to deal additional Malice DMG. A flock of birds sweeps across the sky, their shadows falling upon the earth like fate itself.","m":["Fleeting Shadow: 1st Instance DMG Ratio: 23%","Fleeting Shadow: 2nd Instance DMG Ratio: 48% ×2","Fleeting Shadow: 3rd Instance DMG Ratio: 30% ×4","Fleeting Shadow: 4th Instance DMG Ratio: 25% ×5","Fleeting Shadow: 5th Instance DMG Ratio: 36% ×5"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Netherplume Rite","d":"Netherplume Rite Uses Chain Cage to deal Psyche DMG to the target and inflict a Forsaken Feather mark on targets hit for a set duration. Casts to gain Malice . While Forsaken Feather is active, triggers Forsaken Bird to perform a coordinated attack when another active ally deals DMG to the marked target. Forsaken Bird deals Psyche DMG in an area around the target. Triggers no more than once every 2s , up to 5 times in total. Flames of Deliverance Charges toward the target at high speed while Blackbird is in the Witch of Deliverance state, dealing Psyche DMG . Consumes Malice after hitting an enemy. Activation: Activates after Witch of Deliverance performs the 5th hit of Pyreflame or casts No Quarter. This skill is inactive by default. To the fire, flesh and bone; to the sky, feather and claw.","m":["Netherplume Rite DMG Ratio: 100% ×4","Forsaken Bird: Coordinated Attack DMG Ratio: 200%","Flames of Deliverance DMG Ratio: 105% ×4","Netherplume Rite Cooldown: 16s","Forsaken Feather Duration: 15s"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Requies Animarum","d":"Requies Animarum Transforms into the Witch of Deliverance and launches multiple attacks, dealing massive Psyche DMG to the target. Gains Hitstun Immunity and increases Movement Speed while in the Witch of Deliverance state, which lasts for a set duration. Reverts to Blackbird when the duration ends. The duration does not decrease while she is off-field. Increases the entire team\u0027 ATK after casting Requies Animarum. Flammae in Unum Exits the Witch of Deliverance state and launches multiple attacks against the target, dealing massive Psyche DMG . The sky was black as ink, and birds fell like rain.","m":["Requies Animarum DMG Ratio: 46% ×9","Flammae in Unum DMG Ratio: 90% ×7","Requies Animarum Cooldown: 20s","Witch of Deliverance Duration: 16s","Ultimate Energy Cost: 100"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Judgment Upon Me","d":"Judgment Upon Me The bird will deliver everything it finds to me. Transforms into Lonesome Bird and deals Psyche DMG to the target. Gains Malice after hitting an enemy. Naught but Mercy Accept the Witch\u0027s blessing. Deals Psyche DMG while in the Witch of Deliverance state. Consumes Malice after hitting an enemy. He came to this land and blessed the earth. And the people praised Him, sang of Him, sustained Him, and fed upon Him. \"Ah! What a selfless savior He is!\"","m":["Judgment Upon Me DMG Ratio: 200%","Naught but Mercy DMG Ratio: 200%","Malice Cost by Naught but Mercy: 1.7"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Thrushsong","d":"Stain Enhancement : Increases Stain\u0027s base DMG Bonus to 30% and extends its duration to 20s . Nova Enhancement : When Nova ends, deals additional Mental DMG equal to 20% of the actual total DMG taken by the target while Nova was active (excluding DMG dealt by the Support Skill that triggered Nova and by Nova itself), up to 1,000× Blackbird\u0027s Base ATK. This additional DMG is not affected by any other DMG Buffs or Debuffs. Inflicts Nova on the target once afterward. Prevents Nova inflicted by this effect from triggering the Nova reapplication effect again. \"All over. All done. All over. All done. We are dying. We are dying.\"","m":[]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Ever Onward","d":"Grants 20 Malice when Blackbird casts Judgment Upon Me. \"A hundred years to wander, a hundred years to fly, a hundred years to seek, a hundred years to sing.\"","m":[]}],"how":"Blackbird-Daffodill-Sakiri-Haniel A Blackbird main DPS team that focuses on triggering Nova as much as possible. Sakiri and Haniel provide ATK buffs while Daffodill enables Nova cycles and provides additional damage via her Phantom Steps. Sakiri: Use Ultimate and then Redirect Skill, then swap to Blackbird. Blackbird: Use Redirect Skill, then swap to Daffodill to trigger Nova. Daffodil: Use Ultimate and then Redirect Skill, then swap to Haniel. Haniel: Use Ultimate and then Redirect Skill, then swap to Blackbird. Blackbird: Use the 1st Ultimate, then continue to Basic Attack until her enhanced Redirect Skill is ready. The enhanced Redirect Skill is unlocked after Blackbird performs the 5th hit in her Basic Attack chain or a Perfect Counter. Blackbird: Use the enhanced Redirect Skill, then hold Basic Attack to use her Charged Attack. Blackbird: Continue to Basic Attack until her enhanced Redirect Skill is ready, then repeat the previous step. Try to use three enhanced Redirect Skills during the Ultimate. Blackbird: Use the 2nd Ultimate, then Basic Attack 5 times to generate Malice and prepare for the next rotation. After finishing the Basic Attacks, swap to Daffodill to trigger Nova. Daffodill: Use Redirect skill, then swap to Sakiri. Sakiri: Use Ultimate and then Redirect Skill, then swap to Blackbird. Blackbird: Use Redirect skill, then swap to Daffodill to trigger Nova. Daffodill: Use Ultimate if available, otherwise swap to Haniel. Haniel: Use Ultimate and then Redirect Skill, then swap to Blackbird. From here, use Blackbird’s 1st Ultimate and repeat the steps above starting from when Blackbird used her Ultimate for the first time. Tips \u0026 Tricks You can click Blackbird’s Basic Attack during the animation of her 1st Ultimate to make her start the Basic Attack chain from the 3rd hit once her Ultimate animation ends. This will save a bit of time and help unlock her enhanced Redirect Skill earlier. Always use Blackbird’s 2nd Ultimate instead of letting the duration run out. Blackbird’s 2nd Ultimate is essentially extra damage with no downsides. In the event that the boss moves around a lot, it might be beneficial to swap off of Blackbird to not waste her Ultimate uptime and also proc more instances of her coordinated attack. Blackbird’s Ultimate duration will be paused when she is not on-field.","pros":"Redirect skill provides an instant cycle, providing the team with another Esper Cycle every rotation. Very versatile kit with high personal damage, off-field coordinated attacks that generate a small amount of energy and a teamwide damage buff. Has both Nova and Stain enhancements, allowing her to fit into a variety of teams as either main DPS or sub DPS. Nova enhancement in particular buffs team damage and enables more frequent Discord triggers. Can turn into a crow and fly at high speed in the overworld, making exploration a lot more convenient (can collect Oracle Stones in the crow form too). Immune to interruptions during ultimate transformation state. High damage and skill ceiling with swap-cancelling rotations. Barefoot.","cons":"Enhanced skill needs to be unlocked by basic attack chain; dodging will delay the rotation slightly Combat kit cannot be fully utilised at A0 without swap cancelling; both main DPS and sub DPS playstyles will result in certain parts of her kit being underutilised when using a simple rotation Flying in the crow form consumes stamina and she cannot open the glider once stamina runs out.","teams":[{"n":"Nova Team","m":["sakiri","daffodil","haniel, fadia"],"c":"Blackbird is the main DPS in this team and the goal is to trigger Nova as much as possible by switching to Daffodill whenever Blackbird has full cycle energy. Daffodil will provide additional damage and break without taking up too much time, leaving the majority of on-field time to Blackbird. Haniel and Sakiri will provide ATK buffs for the team, with the addition of crowd control from Sakiri and ATK reduction on the enemy from Haniel.","r":""},{"n":"Stain Team","m":["chaos, hathor","daffodil","sakiri, iroi"],"c":"This is another variation of a Blackbird main DPS team where both Stain and Nova will be triggered. Any available Lakshana character works, although they lack proper synergy with Blackbird outside of their Lakshana identity. Daffodill will enable Nova, faster breaks and provide additional damage with minimal on-field time, whereas Sakiri will provide ATK buffs and crowd control for the team.","r":""},{"n":"SubDPS","m":["zankou","lacrimosa, daffodil","linko, sakiri"],"c":"The main goal of this team is to break the enemy as quickly as possible. Once Scorch is triggered, it will exist throughout the fight due to Zankou’s Scorch enhancement, which causes every trigger of Nova to also trigger Discord. Daffodil provides extra break efficiency via her Discord enhancement, which reduces the maximum break gauge of the enemy so they enter the broken state more often. Linko’s ultimate, redirect skill and follow-up attacks w","r":""}]},"Lacrimosa":{"slug":"lacrimosa","skills":[{"t":"Basic Attack","n":"Sweet and Sour","d":"Basic Attack: Tomato Metal Swings her Frying Pan, performing up to 5 consecutive attacks, dealing Chaos DMG . The projectile generated by the 2nd attack can be shattered by subsequent attacks, causing an explosion and dealing extra Chaos DMG . Basic Attack: Tomato Percussion Manipulates Red Jelly, performing up to 5 consecutive attacks, dealing Chaos DMG . Flavor Variation Flavor Variation can be used at any time via the Aim button. Tosses her Frying Pan and performs a flying kick forward when using Tomato Metal, dealing 1 instance of Chaos DMG to each target hit. Switches her attack module to Tomato Percussion. Leaps into the air and slams the ground, dealing 1 instance of AoE Chaos DMG when using Tomato Percussion. Switches her attack module to Tomato Metal. The current Basic Attack style determines the attack pattern of Working Day Judgement. Basic Attack: Devilish Inspiration Hold to enter Aim mode. Deals 1 instance of Chaos DMG to an enemy in the crosshair and learns their combat technique. Temporarily forgets Morning Tomato and uses the learned technique upon successful learning. Learned techniques are stored permanently in Lacrimosa\u0027s memory. New techniques can be learned to replace existing ones, or Lacrimosa can actively forget a technique on the Skill page to recall Morning Tomato. Basic Attack: Lycopersicum Meteors Manipulates Esper Ability Constructs in the air and plunges, dealing 1 instance of Chaos DMG to an area upon impact. Increases DMG based on fall height, up to 100% . Critical Riposte: fff Rest Triggers when using Basic Attacks after a Critical Dodge. Seizes the opening created by the enemy\u0027s missed attack and violently hurls a large amount of Red Jelly onto the enemy\u0027s head, dealing 6 instances of Chaos DMG to an area and reducing Break. Nightmare Inflicts Nightmare on the target when attacks hit, up to 10 stacks. Inflicts 1 stack of Nightmare per damage instance when a single Basic Attack deals multiple instances of damage. At first, there were no roads. Then Lacrimosa made lots of vehicles and road signs, and suddenly roads appeared. The problem? Too many signs with contradictory rules. How are you supposed to turn left and right at the same time?","m":["Melee Basic Attack: 1st Instance Ratio: 64.2% + 23.2%","Melee Basic Attack: 2nd Instance Ratio: 19.9% ×2","Melee Basic Attack: 3rd Instance Ratio: 24.6% + 14.7% ×3","Melee Basic Attack: 4th Instance Ratio: 70.9% + 27.3%","Melee Basic Attack: 5th Instance Ratio: 23.3% ×3 + 123.3%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Morning Tomato","d":"Skill: Morning Tomato Ah… Achoo! Throws a barrage of unfinished Esper Ability Constructs, dealing 1 instance of Chaos DMG to all targets within the area and inflicting Nightmare on the targets. Combos on the 5th instance of Tomato Metal or Tomato Percussion after casting Morning Tomato. Redirect Skill: Devilish Gift Lacrimosa... can do it too. Lacrimosa uses her Esper Ability to copy and cast an enemy\u0027s skill, triggering the corresponding additional effects. The skill duration matches that of the original owner. During the cast, Lacrimosa cannot move, but she can manually cancel the cast or switch to another character. Lacrimosa takes damage if she is attacked during the cast. Casting Devilish Gift grants Lacrimosa a percentage of the original skill owner\u0027s ATK. \"Ah, Lacrimosa… didn\u0027t mean to…\" \"Haha, nice work there, Mosa! Let\u0027s have Skia buy you some ice cream!\" \"Baicang, nosy: ice cream — three scoops…\"","m":["Morning Tomato DMG Ratio: 300%","Morning Tomato Nightmare Stacks: 5 stacks","Devilish Gift ATK Gain: 30%","Devilish Gift Max ATK Gain: 200","Devilish Gift Min ATK Gain: 10"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Working Day Judgement","d":"Controls the Truck when using Tomato Metal, dealing 10 instances of Chaos DMG to an area and inflicting Nightmare on all targets in range. Dismantles the Car when using Tomato Percussion, dealing 5 instances of Chaos DMG to an area and inflicting Nightmare on all targets in range. A friendly reminder from Barracuda, BAC\u0027s Professional Maintenance Staff: ETD-4 has exhausted their free maintenance quota for this month. Future repair costs will be deducted from the performance bonus of those who file the requests. CERTAIN team members are kindly reminded to take better care of Bureau property, especially non-reinforced glass items and sensitive electronic equipment. CERTAIN team members needing items from the vending machine should seek assistance from their squad captain or lieutenant.","m":["Truck DMG Ratio: 253.3% ×2 + 42.7% ×5 + 93.3% ×3","Car DMG Ratio: 94.2% ×4 + 623.3%","Inflicts Nightmare: 5 stacks","CD: 30s","Ultimate Energy Cost: 120"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Microwake","d":"Lacrimosa get this done, and Lacrimosa get to sleep — Manipulates Esper Ability Constructs, dealing 1 instance of Chaos DMG to an area. Lacrimosa couldn\u0027t care less about villain arcs and tragic backstories. She just wants to clock out and go home to sleep.","m":["DMG Ratio: 200%"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Tomato Banquet","d":"Discord Enhancement : Deals additional DMG equal to 400% of ATK to the target when Discord is triggered, if the target is already Broken. Weekday morning alarms… magic, mess with memory. \"So this is your excuse for being late?\" \"Alarm 1, Alarm 2, Lacrimosa turned them all off. But… ah… Lacrimosa can\u0027t remember…\"","m":[]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Sleep In","d":"Grants 1 additional attempt of Morning Tomato after Lacrimosa uses Tomato Metal or Tomato Percussion 5 times during the skill cooldown. Activates only 1 time per skill cooldown. One person\u0027s sweet dream can be another\u0027s nightmare. Makes you wonder… why don\u0027t people wake themselves up with their sleep talking?","m":[]}],"how":"Lacrimosa Quickswap Lacrimosa · Haniel · Sakiri · Daffodill This team allows Lacrimosa to get her Discord proc and reduce enemies\u0027 max break bar, leading to easier breaks with each Discord reaction. With both Lacrimosa and Daffodill on the team, it also provides the opportunity to proc Scorch and Nova from either character. Rotation Haniel: Use her Redirect Skill (Silent Moonlit Forest Guardian) and then her Ultimate (A Melody Named Haniel) to apply ATK buffs to the team. Sakiri: Use her Ultimate to apply her ATK buff, then use her Redirect Skill (Devour Whole) to gain energy. Daffodill: Use her Ultimate (Finale) and Redirect Skill (Resonance), then Swap-Cancel during her skill animation. Lacrimosa: Use her transform Redirect Skill (Devilish Gift / Morning Tomato), then Swap-Cancel during the animation to Sakiri. Sakiri: Swap in to proc Scorch, then swap back to Lacrimosa once Scorch is applied. Lacrimosa: Execute Basic Attack string hits 1 through 5. During Basic 5, swap to Daffodill. Daffodill: Use her enhanced Basic Attack (Phantom Step), then Swap-Cancel back to Lacrimosa. Lacrimosa: Use her Redirect Skill (Devilish Gift / Morning Tomato) to push to Basic 5. During Basic 5, swap back to Daffodill. Daffodill: Use her second Phantom Step, then swap back to Haniel to restart the rotation. If Haniel and Sakiri are not yet at max energy, hold off and repeat the sub-rotation until they are. Tips \u0026 Tricks Save the Discord reaction for when the enemy is Broken for extra damage from Lacrimosa\u0027s reaction enhancement. You can also use it to damage the break bar more quickly with Daffodill\u0027s Discord enhancement. Lacrimosa\u0027s Ranged Basic 1–4 deals more DPS than the Melee combo 1–4, but the Melee combo Basic 5 is faster. When using her Redirect Skill to store Basic 5, it is best to be in Melee mode. The 5th hit of Lacrimosa\u0027s Melee and Ranged Basic Attack combo, along with all of her transform Redirect Skills, can be Swap Cancelled. Lacrimosa\u0027s Ranged Basic 4 can be Dodge Cancelled as soon as the lollipops appear. For Lacrimosa to swap between Ranged and Melee modes, the full animation of the swap must complete.","pros":"Good at both ST and AoE scenarios. Wide kit, with a high variety of ways to approach gameplay. Can still be useful as a cycle enabler and off-field DPS (through DoTs) if she has at least one dupe. The passive that increases the amount of income from Pink Paws Heist helps considerably with the grind.","cons":"Doesn’t offer any utility to the team outside of damage unless she has her A6. She demands too much field time to build stacks and do her job compared to most other DPS characters, unless she has dupes.","teams":[{"n":"Discord Team","m":["sakiri","daffodil","haniel"],"c":"This team allows Lacrimosa to get her Discord proc and reduce the enemies’ max break bar; leading to easier breaks with each Discord reaction. With both her and Daffofill on the team, it also provides the opportunity to proc Scorch and Nova from either character.","r":""},{"n":"ETD-4 DoT Team","m":["sakiri","baicang","fadia"],"c":"This team focuses on cycling all the Incantation units with Lacrimosa to stack and maintain Scorch.","r":""}]},"Skia":{"slug":"skia","skills":[{"t":"Basic Attack","n":"Arresting Art","d":"Basic Attack: Arresting Art Performs up to 5 consecutive attacks using steady martial arts techniques, dealing Lakshana DMG . Splits 1 Fang Thrust from his shadow to pursue each target hit. Locks each target with up to 3 Fang Thrusts simultaneously. Basic Attack: Territory Control Strikes in the air and plunges, dealing 1 instance of Lakshana DMG to an area upon impact. Increases DMG based on fall height, up to 100% . Fang Thrust Splitting from Skia\u0027s shadow, these shattered shadows resemble the fangs of a giant beast. They automatically track and attach to targets, disappearing after dealing 1 instance of Lakshana DMG . Critical Riposte: Pen to Paper Triggers when using Arresting Art after a Critical Dodge. Strikes enemies with ink-splash shadows, dealing 1 instance of Lakshana DMG to an area and reducing Break. \"The doggo… This dark stuff comes out with doggo punches… pretty impressive.\"","m":["1st Instance Ratio: 30.4%","2nd Instance Ratio: 3.7% ×2 + 18.9%","3rd Instance Ratio: 32.1% + 45.9%","4th Instance Ratio: 39.1%","5th Instance Ratio: 29.4% + 55.4%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Shadow Hound Chase","d":"A workflow designed for pursuit. Enters the Tailed state, leaps into own shadow, and deals 6 instances of Lakshana DMG to an area. Splits 3 Fang Thrusts from shadow for each target hit, then enters Shadow Hound Gnaw mode. Tailed Prevents Fang Thrusts from disappearing after dealing damage to targets during the state. Shadow Hound Gnaw Allows movement on ground or wall surfaces, similar to Shadow Hound mode. Remains undetected when approaching enemy targets. Grants immunity to certain attacks, but cancels the mode when hit by ground damage. Triggers additional attacks from Fang Thrusts whenever touching an enemy already marked by them. Press Basic Attack or switch characters to exit this mode during its duration. Moves forward at the edge of a high place to end this mode. Deals 1 instance of Lakshana DMG to an area upon exiting the mode. Some nimble troublemakers might think they can escape ETD\u0027s pursuit… They should check what\u0027s lurking beneath their feet.","m":["Quad Strike DMG Ratio: 30% ×4","Dive DMG Ratio: 4.6% + 25.4%","Tailed Duration: 6s","Fang Thrust Extra DMG Ratio: 55%","Fang Thrust Extra DMG Interval: 0.35s"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"The Pack","d":"A workflow designed for suppression. Throws a spinning lighter, causing his shadow to spread across the ground in all directions, dealing 1 instance of Lakshana DMG to an area. Converges multiple shadows on a single location like well-trained canines, dealing 3 instances of Lakshana DMG to an area. Increases Fang Thrust\u0027s damage after casting The Pack (including collision damage in Shadow Hound Gnaw mode) and inflicts a control effect on targets with each attack. The consequences of \"non-compliance.\"","m":["Spread DMG Ratio: 290.2%","Converge DMG Ratio: 69.9% ×3","Fang Thrust DMG Up: 10%","DMG Increase Duration: 15s","Fang Thrust Control Duration: 0.75s"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Arrest Warrant","d":"The relentless shadows cannot be shaken off. Commands the shadow like a police canine to bite the target, dealing 1 instance of Lakshana DMG to an area.","m":["DMG Ratio: 200%"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Suppression","d":"Remora Enhancement : Inflicts an additional Remora on a target when Fang Thrust locks onto them in Remora state. Usually, there\u0027s no need for physical intervention — Skia can subdue targets with just his shadows, keeping facilities undamaged. Plus, he helps with cleanup… According to a BAC cafeteria survey, 84% of staff welcome Skia at their work site — less hassle for them!","m":[]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Apprehension","d":"Increases Fang Thrust damage by 10% for 15 s after casting The Pack, including collision damage in Shadow Hound Gnaw mode. Your body might be free to move, but your shadow is held in an iron grip, rendering you immobile… Quite the peculiar sensation.","m":[]}],"how":"Skia Hyper Skia · Zero (MC) · Haniel · Jiuyuan A Remora-Charge stealth team built around Skia\u0027s Fang Thrust stacking in Shadow Hound Gnaw mode, synergizing with Zero\u0027s Blossom and Jiuyuan for the Charge triple-cycle. Rotation Jiuyuan: Start with Jiuyuan and use her Ultimate (Final Reckoning) and Redirect Skill. Zero (MC): Switch to MC to trigger Blossom and use their Ultimate. Haniel: Switch to Haniel and use her Redirect Skill (Silent Moonlit Forest Guardian) and Ultimate (A Melody Named Haniel) to apply the ATK and Crit Damage buff (at R6). Skia: Swap to Skia to trigger Stain. Zero (MC): Quick-Swap from Skia to MC. Zero (MC): While on MC, use Redirect Skill. Skia: Swap to Skia to trigger Remora and Charge, then use his Redirect Skill (Shadow Hound Chase) followed by his Ultimate (The Pack). Skia: Remain in Shadow Hound Gnaw mode, pursuing Fang Thrust-marked enemies to detonate follow-up damage. Take time rebuilding energy and Cycle bar on Haniel. Repeat from the first step. Tips \u0026 Tricks Skia\u0027s Perfect Dodge needs to be timed precisely; otherwise he will sink into his shadow and still take the hit. When timed properly, his Dodge Counter has one of the longest i-frame windows in the game. Be careful when using Skia\u0027s Ultimate (The Pack) — make sure you are right next to the enemy. The attack is centered on Skia and can easily miss at range. Shadow Hound Chase costs no Stamina, allowing Skia to scale walls and buildings freely. Activating it before enemies detect him keeps them unaware during stealth sections.","pros":"Once Fang Thrust is stacked, his damage starts to feel noticeably stronger A lot of his damage happens automatically after setup, so you are not constantly micromanaging everything Good at pressuring groups of enemies, especially when he is moving through them in shadow form Shop Management buffs.","cons":"Damage can be a bit lower than some other DPS. Even in shadow form, he is not invulnerable, so you still have to be careful when diving in.","teams":[{"n":"Skia Stain Team","m":["zero, hotori","haniel, fadia","hathor"],"c":"This team can trigger both Remora and Stain to buff Skia’s personal damage. The goal would be to trigger Stain and get as much of Skia’s damage under the 20% buff as possible. Hathor also extends Remora and buffs Crit rate with it, allowing Skia to deal even more damage in this window.","r":""},{"n":"Skia Hypercarry Team","m":["haniel","zero, hotori","jiuyuan, nanally, mint"],"c":"This team can trigger both Stain and Charge. Ideally the order you would want to trigger things in is Blossom \u003e Stain \u003e Remora (Charge) with Skia being the one to trigger the Charge reaction. Additionally, you can use this team to trigger Charge first and give Haniel energy for her Ultimate and then switch off of her onto Skia for the maximum Stain duration.","r":""}]},"Shinku":{"slug":"shinku","skills":[{"t":"Basic Attack","n":"Special Combat Arts","d":"Basic Attack: Special Combat Arts Performs up to 5 consecutive attacks, dealing Cosmos DMG . Grants Defiant Spirit on hit. Basic Attack: Arrowfall Press Basic Attack while airborne to plunge, dealing 1 instance of Cosmos DMG upon impact. Increases DMG based on fall height, up to 100% . Basic Attack: Special Combat Arts (Altered) Hold Basic Attack during the 3rd/4th/5th hit of Special Combat Arts to trigger Special Combat Arts (Altered), dealing Cosmos DMG and granting Defiant Spirit on hit. Critical Riposte: Split-Second Victory Triggers when using Special Combat Arts after a Critical Dodge. Retaliates against the target with a sharp kick, dealing 1 instance of Cosmos DMG , reducing their Break, and gaining Defiant Spirit . Basic Attack: Tidal Assault Performs up to 5 consecutive attacks, dealing Cosmos DMG . Grants Fading Reason on hit. Basic Attack: Hammerfall Press Basic Attack while airborne to plunge, dealing 1 instance of Cosmos DMG upon impact. Increases DMG based on fall height, up to 100% . Grants Fading Reason on hit. Basic Attack: Tidal Assault (Scorn) Hold Basic Attack during the 3rd/4th/5th hit of Tidal Assault to trigger Tidal Assault (Scorn), dealing 1 instance of Cosmos DMG and granting Fading Reason on hit. Critical Riposte: No Respite Triggers when using Tidal Assault after a Critical Dodge. Retaliates against the target with a sharp kick, dealing 1 instance of Cosmos DMG , reducing the target\u0027s Break, and gaining Fading Reason . Inflicts Forced Knockback and briefly stuns (not effective against Bosses) the target when Parry Attack or Critical Riposte hits while in the Menacing Gaze state, then deals 1 additional instance of DMG to the target equal to 20% of Instant Strike. \"Tear through metal, smash through walls—when your own limbs are lethal weapons built for both offense and defense, why weigh yourself down with a weapon?\"","m":["Basic Attack: Special Combat Arts 1st Instance DMG Ratio: 18.2%","Basic Attack: Special Combat Arts 2nd Instance DMG Ratio: 30.8% + 20.5%","Basic Attack: Special Combat Arts 3rd Instance DMG Ratio: 29.4% + 17.4% + 19.7% + 42.1%","Basic Attack: Special Combat Arts 4th Instance DMG Ratio: 81.5% + 49.8%","Basic Attack: Special Combat Arts 5th Instance DMG Ratio: 112.9%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"High-Speed Breach","d":"Redirect Skill: High-Speed Breach No time to catch your breath. Charges toward the target and launches a fierce assault, dealing multiple instances of Cosmos DMG and gaining Defiant Spirit . Redirect Skill: Scarlet Descent Consumes all Fading Reason . Leaps above the target into their blind spot and unleashes a powerful downward claw strike, dealing high Cosmos DMG . Casts up to 5 times during each Surging Crimson state. \"Let\u0027s end this quickly, before this gets any worse.\"","m":["DMG Ratio: 17.3% + 23.1% + 79.6%","Redirect Skill: High-Speed Breach grants Defiant Spirit: 5","Redirect Skill: High-Speed Breach Cycle Energy: 9","Required Fading Reason for Redirect Skill: Scarlet Descent: 12","Redirect Skill: Scarlet Descent 1st Instance DMG Ratio: 22.4% + 217.6%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Crimson Fury","d":"Ultimate: Crimson Fury Don\u0027t think you can pull something like that and escape unscathed… Consumes all Defiant Spirit to enter the Surging Crimson state, then launches multiple attacks, dealing high Cosmos DMG to the target. Replaces Special Combat Arts with Tidal Assault and High-Speed Breach with Scarlet Descent while in Surging Crimson state. Increases DMG dealt and Resistance to Interruptions, greatly boosts Movement, and lasts for 13s . Ends Surging Crimson when switching characters. Hold Dodge while moving to partially release her Esper Ability and greatly boost Movement. Ultimate: Crimson Judgment Casts Crimson Judgment when Surging Crimson is about to end. Press Ultimate repeatedly to dash rapidly between targets, dealing high Cosmos DMG . Grants 1 additional instance of Crimson Judgment for each use of Scarlet Descent during Surging Crimson . Can be cast up to 3 times during each Surging Crimson state. Ultimate: Dragonflame Verdict Press Ultimate again to cast Dragonflame Verdict after all uses of Crimson Judgment have been consumed or after Surging Crimson ends, dealing massive Cosmos DMG to targets in a large area. \"It will hurt—for her enemies, and for her as well.\"","m":["Ultimate: Crimson Fury DMG Ratio: 18.5% + 120% + 55% ×5 + 144% + 42.5%","Ultimate: Crimson Judgment Per Instance DMG Ratio: 60% ×4","Ultimate: Dragonflame Verdict DMG Ratio: 20% ×10 + 400%","Increases DMG in Surging Crimson: 30%","Increases Resistance to Interruptions: 50%"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Breaching Tactics","d":"Enough already! Delivers a forceful knee strike, dealing 1 instance of Cosmos DMG and gaining Defiant Spirit . \"For a girl long used to fighting alone, learning to stand beside others marks a major step forward.\"","m":["DMG Ratio: 200%"]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Lone Stride","d":"Charge Enhancement : Grants off-field characters the same amount of Charge when the active character gains Ultimate Energy. While Shinku is active and in Charge state, each trigger deals AoE DMG equal to 400% of ATK (scales with Basic Attack level, reaching 863.6% at level 11), and increases her ATK by 5% for 30s , up to 10 stacks. Cooldown: 1s . \"For Shinku as she is now, few situations are enough to make her go all out.\"","m":[]},{"t":"Support Skill","n":"Wrathscale","d":"Increases Ultimate DMG against non-Boss enemies by 50% . \"—Unless her friends are in peril.\"","m":[]}],"how":"Rotation If cycle gauge is needed, start on Shinku and use 8 stacks on skill and then 4 stacks on skill or dodge counter to fill her cycle gauge. Hathor: Switch Hathor to trigger Remora and use her Ultimate and Redirect Skill. Zero (MC): During Hathor’s skill animation, switch to MC and use their Ultimate and then skill. Nanally: Swap to Nanally during Zero’s skill animation, triggering Blossom and Charge. Use Nanally’s Ultimate and then Redirect Skill. Shinku: Switch to Shinku during Nanally’s skill and use her Ultimate. Charge should be ongoing during her Ultimate State. Shinku: Use Shinku’s basic attack once or twice, until her enhanced skill gauge is filled and then use her enhanced skill. Repeat this for a total of 5 times. Her Ult dashes should be available at this point, use 3 of them. This will lead to her Ult finisher and deal big damage to the enemy. Shinku: After she exits her Ult, stay on field with her to get 8 stacks and then use her skill and switch off. Repeat from the beginning, keeping in mind that if you spend too much time on characters that aren’t Skinku she might run out of her stacking attack buff or not be able to get all of her enhanced skills during her Ultimate. Tips \u0026 Tricks Shinku gains a tremendous amount for being on field while Charge is occurring, aim to do this as much as possible. Unlike some other characters, she does need to be on field for her reaction enhancement to activate. During Shinku’s downtime, the goal is to get 8 stacks of “her stacks“, since doing this is more dps than actually doing her full basic attack rotation twice. You can advance Shinku’s stack gain more quickly by perfect dodging enemy attacks, and spending 8 stacks on a critical riposte provides additional damage.","pros":"Massive Ultimate damage that serves as the main payoff of her entire kit. Simple gameplan, you build up her Defiant Spirit easily just by attacking, with holding Basic Attack, Critical Riposte, Redirect Skill, and Support Skill all contributing towards that. Strong team utility through Charge Enhancement, providing off-field energy sharing and frequent AOE triggers while also stacking self ATK up to 10 times. Buffs for Owner Selection with 3 tags focused on drinks, plus buffs for Mahjong that consume more city stamina so you can finish faster.","cons":"QoL features such as full interrupt resistance and retaining stacks after switching are locked behind Awakenings so she can feel more clunky than expected. Very reliant on Charge to reach her maximum damage potential. Relies on the boss staying targetable or within range to deal most of her damage. If you setup for Shinku\u0027s Ultimate and then the boss leaves, it is very punishing. Her abilities ungroup enemies often, and you can\u0027t switch off of her during her Ultimate to re-gather them otherwise you would lose it.","teams":[{"n":"Shinku Charge","m":["zero, hotori","hathor, skia","iroi, jiuyuan, nanally, mint"],"c":"Shinku\u0027s Charge team focuses on quickly getting Charge setup and going into Shinku to maximize her damage during her Ultimate state. We are aiming for 5 enhanced skills and 3 dashes during each Ult, and this team leads to that more consistently than most.","r":""},{"n":"Shinku Dual DPS","m":["chaos","nanally, jiuyuan, mint","hathor"],"c":"This dual DPS team utilizes both Shinku and Chaos and aims to maximize the damage that occurs while Shinku is off field and/or outside of her Ultimate state.","r":""}]}};